{
  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading guide: task-replacement series (17 files)\\n\\n**Where I looked:** all 17 files under `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/`.\\n\\n**Coverage gaps:**\\n- The plan (64,964 bytes) and r32 (12,058 bytes) exceeded the display cap. I read their top sections in full. For the later sections I used line-numbered search with context, so a few long lines (plan lines 62, 75, 79, 83, 85, 89, 95, 112, 116, 130, 136, 138, 140, 144, 396 and the tail of 405) were cut off mid-sentence.\\n- I did not read the plan's module-by-module removal tables (about lines 193–333). I saw only their headings and a few rows.\\n- Nothing in the series gives a date except the plan's 2026-10-13 preflight and Oct 14 target, and r32's \\\"October 15 source progress\\\". \\\"Status\\\" below is what each file says about itself.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. `task-replacement-plan.md` (revision R2), group: Foundation contract\\n- **Status:** target release Oct 14 (America/Chicago). Preflight receipt dated 2026-10-13. The target is explicitly not permission to bypass acceptance.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Delete the old task integration first, then rebuild around one typed `TaskSnapshot`, one confirmed Core writer and one recipient-input record as the only delivery acknowledgement.\\n  - Native execution goes through FastMCP/Docket. The pinned tuple is FastMCP/fastmcp-tasks 4.1.0, MCP 2.0.0, Docket 0.26.2.\\n  - The conversation engine alone decides assignment transitions. Relay becomes an ordinary MCP server.\\n  - No old-engine fallback, stubs or archives. A deliberately broken removal commit stays local with draft PRs.\\n  - Acceptance is gated on Q1–Q9 live families, six races (R1–R6) repeated five times each, CI, and migration idempotence.\\n- **Builds on:** baseline core `5475042f` / GACT `32044a38`, and the protected human design docs (`subagent-lifecycle-and-session-messaging.md`, `agent-task-architecture-review-2026-10-12.md`, `session-recall-and-long-term-memory.md`). Later sections cite removal reviews and \\\"R30\\\" Astra review.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - If gates fail, no release.\\n  - Provider-continuation reattachment was pending implementation and Claude source review (line 405).\\n  - Local-transfer interruption is an explicit migration/native-recovery requirement (W01/N12).\\n  - Relay migration is explicitly not promised.\\n  - Startup-replay and performance optimizations are deferred to measurement (Q8).\\n  - Live-model availability was only a credentials check, not acceptance.\\n\\n## 2. `task-replacement-corrections-r19.md`, group: Retained-behavior corrections\\n- **Status:** packet addressing Astra R17 and Claude R18. Behavioral tests held until initial implementation.\\n- **Decided:** eight corrections C1–C8 within existing owners:\\n  - Restore an absent same-session context from validated evidence only.\\n  - Route every plan-Question close through one resolver.\\n  - Resolve stale Question answers against historical identities.\\n  - Bind pause holds to their assignment.\\n  - Resume workflows from saved checkpoints.\\n  - Add an owner-local workflow deadline timer.\\n  - Allow linked workflow retry.\\n  - Keep strict settlement for unknown external cancellation.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, the Astra and Claude R17/R18 reviews, and the reports `task-replacement-correction-plan-astra-r19.md` / `-claude-r19.md`.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - An optional human decision on amending R2 to allow an authenticated restart past unresolved cancellation. This is pending and not implemented.\\n  - Short-control Core cost (Q8).\\n  - Claude's suggestion to count external acknowledgement as settlement was rejected, not adopted.\\n\\n## 3. `task-replacement-corrections-r21.md`, group: Retained-behavior corrections\\n- **Status:** completes the R20 source-review set. Frozen base core `f020a591`, GACT `ce993164`, marketplace `9257bba5`. Both reviewers returned NO-GO. All production corrections are initially implemented. Behavioral cases are constructed but unexecuted.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Context-recovery boundaries.\\n  - Per-assignment pause recovery.\\n  - Deadline applied at deferred Stop-hook completion.\\n  - Workflow identity/historical lookup via provenance and passive indexes.\\n  - Workflow state handoff between steps.\\n  - Passive (non-self-cancelling) observation callbacks.\\n  - Retirement of finished native/external bindings.\\n  - Isolated per-session plan-gate repair.\\n  - Idempotent approval retry.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, R19, and the R20 reports in `docs/qualification/task-replacement-implementation-*-r20.md`.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - The human restart-despite-unresolved-cancellation decision is still pending.\\n  - Short-control/Core performance needs measurement.\\n  - Failed, skipped and unavailable gates stay unqualified.\\n  - Both reviewers' source approval is still required.\\n\\n## 4. `task-replacement-corrections-r23.md`, group: Retained-behavior corrections\\n- **Status:** combined R22 correction packet, base core `b9765992`. Both reviewers returned source NO-GO. The packet is initially implemented, with no source approval or CI claimed.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Retain the exact failed cancellation request.\\n  - Insert uncertain observations before orphan closure.\\n  - Allow an empty historical workflow request string.\\n  - Add a conversation-owned context-clear epoch.\\n  - Freeze plan-resolution content in the Question.\\n  - Retire obsolete cancellation delivery at shutdown.\\n  - Dedupe external attention.\\n  - Isolate workflow recovery per root.\\n  - Exclude the current input row from restoration.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, R19–R21, and `task-replacement-correction-seams-astra-r23.md`.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - The optional human amendment is unanswered.\\n  - Regression construction and legacy fixture migration are unexecuted.\\n  - CI, migration and Q1–Q9/R1–R6 remain gates.\\n  - It lists lower-severity observations to check in the next review.\\n\\n## 5. `task-replacement-corrections-r26.md`, group: Boundary tightening\\n- **Status:** addresses Astra R24 and Claude Code Fable R25. It explicitly does not approve its own corrections.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Shared GACT aliases and run-state decoder.\\n  - Await worker result instead of polling threads.\\n  - Named reads and writes on the history writer instead of private-map access.\\n  - Typed owner-observation fields validated at the writer.\\n  - Index-seeded exact/active queries.\\n  - Bounded health-ping timeout.\\n  - Preserve fresh-context epoch in migration.\\n  - Capture the resolved primary agent.\\n  - Refuse local admission of historical non-local conversations.\\n  - Unwind partial native startup.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, and the R24/R25 reviews.\\n- **Left open:** \\\"Fresh proof still required\\\" for each row. Q1–Q9, R1–R6, CI, migration and real-model evidence remain mandatory, and old evidence does not qualify this packet. Both reviewers must assess the committed candidate.\\n\\n## 6. `task-replacement-corrections-r27.md`, group: Boundary tightening\\n- **Status:** review of core `8f40aa8d` / GACT `557aecd3` returned NO-GO. Fable supports the architecture and finds it simpler.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Validate every collected member and reject incomplete observation acknowledgements in the writer.\\n  - Bound the cancellation RPC.\\n  - Forward the REST result cursor.\\n  - Validate ownership before control effects.\\n  - Clear resolved attention only after rechecking evidence.\\n  - Keep the `return_when=\\\"any\\\"` contract unchanged. Baseline `5475042f` used \\\"settled or errors\\\", and R2 did not authorize changing it.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, baseline `5475042f`, and the R26 boundary family (eleven selected cases pass).\\n- **Left open:** unrelated-session growth, final integrated races, CI and Q1–Q9 are separate gates. The retained history case measured 1,004 tasks, 6.631 s replay, 2 exact-query snapshot reads and 9 active-query reads. Reviewer reports are omitted from the Fable package.\\n\\n## 7. `task-replacement-r32-corrections.md`, group: Stop/input/UI\\n- **Status:** \\\"correction map after independent R31 review\\\" (core `3d929627`, GACT `30df56ed`). It includes an \\\"October 15 source progress\\\" section, with test-isolation commits `c6ff3b8c` and `72e7993a`.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Stop reconciliation bound to reservation retirement.\\n  - Release the Question gate for an applied Stop completion.\\n  - Pause-independent gate cleanup.\\n  - Authorized-read-handle answer media.\\n  - Indexed admission.\\n  - Replace the Runs/relay UI with common task controls.\\n  - Use the recipient's own principal for subscriptions.\\n  - Pure cursor validation.\\n  - Input-lifetime rules for Stop, retry and cancel withdrawal, with correlation persisted in the Core mailbox.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, the R31 Astra/Claude reports, and the human's submitted-feedback contract.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - TypeScript, behavior execution, renewed source review, CI and live acceptance are pending.\\n  - Windows-target Mypy is not accepted.\\n  - Ambiguous historical input ownership is not guessed.\\n  - Keep idempotent collection publication unless replaced.\\n  - The marketplace snapshot must be fixed in the next Fable review.\\n  - Tests and Core run only from the D: repository.\\n\\n## 8. `task-replacement-r33-corrections.md`, group: Stop/input/UI\\n- **Status:** reviewed production core `a529569d` / GACT `458313c3`, with test-only follow-ups. Both R32 reviewers accepted the ownership direction and rejected source readiness.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Typed `TaskAccessDenied` leaves a protected observation uncommitted without stranding human input.\\n  - Unsubscribe no longer invalidates an authorized read.\\n  - Read/observe requirements are carried through the short MCP call.\\n  - Passive ordered streams with bounded pages, sparse pages allowed, and unknown totals null.\\n  - Content reads happen outside the writer lock.\\n  - Question retry uses an immutable request reference.\\n  - Malformed durable input is held as `invalid_queued_input`.\\n  - Wait/get-result are annotated as effectful.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, R32, and Astra's pagination conditions in the qualification reports.\\n- **Left open:** R33 behavior tests, fresh source approval, F03, CI and Q1–Q9/R1–R6 are not accepted. Marketplace CI against moving `develop` is only a compatibility signal. It adds no relay qualification.\\n\\n## 9. `task-replacement-r34-corrections.md`, group: Stop/input/UI\\n- **Status:** architecture frozen at R2. R34 source is uncommitted and not accepted. Twenty-six selected R33 cases passed, with three initial failures retained.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Handle only typed access denial.\\n  - Preserve observe-only/uncertain permission in the wait wrapper.\\n  - Runs no longer calls a partial workflow completed.\\n  - Paginated compatibility projections.\\n  - Reuse the child address for the same trusted spawn identity.\\n  - Correct Question guidance.\\n  - Observation without a pattern stays non-blocking, with no long-poll.\\n  - An ungated model-segment error finishes the assignment as failed.\\n- **Builds on:** R33, R2, and the \\\"Test filesystem boundary\\\" rules (D: qualification repo).\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - Native admission-lock contention is advisory and unmeasured.\\n  - 39 absent-import test modules still need mapping.\\n  - The old hard-drain assertion needs migration.\\n  - F03, CI, Q1–Q9 and R1–R6 remain pending.\\n\\n## 10. `task-replacement-r35-corrections.md`, group: Startup/initialization\\n- **Status:** two confirmed R34 defects, implemented but unexecuted.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - SessionStore keeps bounded initialization receipts, so a reused child does not skip known unfinished initialization. A hook admitted without a completion receipt stays uncertain and is never replayed.\\n  - Load-more errors reach the existing error surface through the observability query owner.\\n- **Builds on:** R34, and the established Stop and any-wait contracts, which it preserves.\\n- **Left open:** missing legacy hook receipts mean unknown effects. Exactly-once external effects are not claimed. No R34/R35 b",
  "truncated": true
}

