  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading guide: nine design docs in `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/`\\n\\n**Coverage caveat.** Shell was blocked (read-only session), so I read with `fs_read_file` and `fs_search_text`. Each of those caps output (`fs_read_file` at 12,000 characters, and `fs_search_text` cuts long lines at about 500 characters), so I did not read four files in full.\\n\\nI read these in full:\\n- `task-transcript-coordination.md`\\n- `steering-delivery-order.md`\\n- `agent-question-modes.md`\\n- `agent-driven-elicitation-and-mrtr.md`\\n- `agent-communication-campaign-notes.md`\\n\\nI read these only partly:\\n- **`agent-task-native-v3.md`:** I read lines 1–160 of about 165. Several long lines (for example 69, 72, 76, 78, 80, 134, 145) were cut at about 500 characters.\\n- **`agent-facing-async-tasks.md`:** I read about lines 1–302, 303–365 and 365–551 as long-line excerpts, and about 727–815. I did not read about lines 551–727 (the qualification sub-sections from \\\"Subsequent actual-model task guidance and input recovery\\\" through the start of \\\"Fresh Claude verification and malformed tool output\\\").\\n- **`turn-transcript.md`:** I read lines 1–~190, 361–487, and the \\\"problem\\\" and \\\"invariant\\\" sections. I did not read §3.3, §4, §5 and §6 (PR-by-PR migration, about lines 189–360).\\n- **`subagent-lifecycle-and-session-messaging.md`:** I read lines 1–~232 (one gap) and 232–386. I did not read \\\"Pause, Stop, cancel and restart\\\" and \\\"Proposed model-facing controls\\\" (about lines 250–310) except their first lines.\\n\\nStatements below come from what I read. Where a file's open items might sit in an unread region, I say so.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Topic group A: Agent-facing async tasks (core contract and replacement)\\n\\n### 1. `agent-task-native-v3.md`\\n- **Status and date:** No date or status line.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Rebuild the task integration around native execution (FastMCP Tasks for Shell/Download/Indexing) and CLIO's conversation engine for agent assignments.\\n  - Keep the shared tools `query_tasks`, `observe_tasks`, `wait_tasks`, `cancel_tasks` and `get_task_result`.\\n  - Add a Question kind: `ask_user` returns a durable handle at once, and `wait_tasks(question_handle)` waits unbounded by default.\\n  - Persist submissions before invoking the backend. Recovery promises honest uncertainty, not exactly-once effects.\\n  - Use one admission path and one Core-backed mailbox per session. Sessions are stable addresses, and `assignment_disposition=\\\"yield\\\"|\\\"complete\\\"` separates a turn ending from an assignment ending.\\n  - Remove, rather than wrap, the old schedulers, wake policies and custody modules (§4).\\n- **Builds on:** The branch `codex/agent-facing-async-tasks` (the work in doc 2), \\\"GACT\\\" and Docket/FastMCP. It builds on the existing question owner, TurnRunner and Core hierarchy and writer. It cites no numbered issues in what I read.\\n- **Open or deferred:**\\n  - The Question extension is \\\"an implementation and qualification gate\\\" to be verified with actual models before it counts as complete.\\n  - Distributed agent hosting \\\"does not qualify\\\" locally. It needs cross-host turn reservation and wake transport.\\n  - Local execution does not survive process loss with the default `memory://` backend.\\n  - Native redelivery can repeat or overlap execution, with no exclusive-execution promise.\\n  - Qualification gates are listed in §5 as required and incomplete until passed.\\n  - Merge, release and install are \\\"separate actions.\\\"\\n- **Supersession:** Positions itself as replacing \\\"the accumulated task integration,\\\" so it supersedes the earlier module graph described in doc 2.\\n\\n### 2. `agent-facing-async-tasks.md`\\n- **Status and date:** Feature-branch document with dated checkpoints (2026-10-10) and a \\\"Historical qualification ledger.\\\" States \\\"Release qualification is incomplete\\\" and that both draft PRs remain drafts.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Defines the user-visible contract: immediate opaque handles, five task kinds, authorization before filtering, unbounded `wait_tasks`, non-consuming query and observe, and a shared delivery guard for results.\\n  - Task completion is an active mailbox event. A busy agent gets results before its next safe iteration, and an idle agent is auto-started with a system-event turn.\\n  - Existing registry, `TaskRecordStore` and `TransferOperation` stay authoritative.\\n  - Legacy agent-only control aliases delegate for one release cycle, then are removed.\\n- **Builds on:** core PR1658 (`a8e1357`) and GACT PR555 (`6bdc2a9`), with review PRs core PR1662 and GACT PR557. It links to doc 6 and says that proposal doesn't make pause or restart generic task actions.\\n- **Open or deferred:** The \\\"Blocking and unverified gates\\\" section lists:\\n  - The oversized provider-SSE parser limit (65,536 bytes) is blocked and must not be bypassed.\\n  - The connected-source Download+Shell subtree route is host-rejected and prohibited.\\n  - Windows native-Core crash causes are not established.\\n  - Nonrecoverable backend-loss and input-recovery qualification are pending.\\n  - Other provider, relay, POSIX and platform routes have not passed the full matrix.\\n  - CI Python 3.12 shard 0 hit the 18-minute limit.\\n  - Fresh live gates are still required after later repairs.\\n  - Manual disk cleanup is an incomplete obligation.\\n  - I did not read lines ~551–727, which may contain further open items.\\n- **Supersession:**\\n  - The automatic idle wake explicitly \\\"supersedes the original next-human-turn-only delivery design.\\\"\\n  - The \\\"Historical qualification ledger\\\" says the current checkpoint above supersedes its pending-gate statements.\\n  - Doc 1 (v3) reframes it as a rebuild.\\n\\n### 3. `task-transcript-coordination.md`\\n- **Status and date:** Human requested this on October 19, 2026. No status line.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Session and transcript access goes through the Tasks surface, with no new mailbox, registry, worker or history store.\\n  - `query_tasks` gains `query` and `message_after`/`message_before`.\\n  - `observe_tasks` gains `view` (`progress|transcript|summary|artifacts`), `history` (`assignment|session`), `limit` and `artifact_id`.\\n  - Transcript pages preserve typed rows, with resumable JSON fragments for large rows.\\n  - A separate mutable `live_snapshot` covers unfinished frames.\\n  - The `memory_*` tools (`session_search`, `session_read_summary`, `session_read_context_frame`) become compatibility aliases for one cycle.\\n- **Builds on:** The existing task and conversation owners, the shared Core mailbox and `send_agent_message`. It cites no issue numbers.\\n- **Open or deferred:**\\n  - It states required acceptance criteria rather than results. Contract tests must be constructed before execution, and live demonstrations are required with Codex/Luna and Claude's bridge.\\n  - Review is \\\"with Claude Opus only.\\\"\\n  - Generating maintained long-term knowledge is called \\\"separate work.\\\"\\n  - It states no further open questions.\\n- **Supersession:** Replaces the `memory_*` family as the primary discovery path. Doc 6's \\\"Find a session, read context, then address it\\\" section describes the pre-change memory tools it supersedes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Topic group B: Subagent lifecycle and messaging\\n\\n### 4. `subagent-lifecycle-and-session-messaging.md`\\n- **Status and date:** \\\"Candidate implementation and qualification in progress, 2026-10-11.\\\" The original audit used core `8feb486c` on `codex/agent-facing-async-tasks`.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Adds `pause_agent`, `resume_agent` and `restart_agent(target, fresh=False)`, built on the existing Subagent registry.\\n  - Adds `message_agent` addressing exact session IDs or task handles. A terminal recipient gets a linked successor.\\n  - Every linked restart carries a bounded, validated briefing of accepted operations. This is meant to prevent replay.\\n  - Human control actions notify the actual immediate owner via the durable mailbox.\\n- **Builds on:** Doc 2's shared task tools and Subagent registry, and the pre-existing `memory_*` tools. Core commits it cites include `abe59c8e` (a Codex replay), `ccc105eb`, `2960d197`, `e7e67bb4`, `a8a5c9fc`, `ad51cd45`. It links to `../qualification/agent-facing-tasks-use-cases.md`, which I did not read.\\n- **Open or deferred:**\\n  - Relay pause and retained-context restart, and peer relay addressing, are \\\"explicitly refused\\\" and \\\"unimplemented and unqualified.\\\"\\n  - Full qualification is incomplete. Failures are recorded: Codex `ccc105eb` failed terminal-mail handling through a successor chain, Claude `2960d197` failed a later spawn request, and Claude `ad51cd45` failed a fourth-successor `get_task_result` step.\\n  - Wording alone is \\\"not a deterministic execution deduplication mechanism.\\\"\\n  - The pre-implementation proposals (lines ~250–310) were not read, and the audit section says session summaries and frame persistence need explicit contracts.\\n  - That same audit says \\\"do not promise historical frame availability after restart.\\\"\\n- **Supersession:** Doc 2 says this work is audited separately and is not a generic task action. Doc 3 supersedes the memory-discovery description. Doc 1 absorbs these behaviors into \\\"the shared conversation lifecycle.\\\"\\n\\n### 5. `steering-delivery-order.md`\\n- **Status and date:** No date or status line.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - A steer is accepted immediately and delivered at the next model boundary.\\n  - After generation, CLIO checks for steering before starting any proposed tool. If a steer was delivered, the tool proposal is discarded, the prose is kept, and the model replans.\\n  - The goal judge uses consumed-steer delivery receipts to interleave human input.\\n  - Pending human input defers goal judging, and stale queued goal wakes are rejected.\\n  - The UI labels reasoning as \\\"Thinking\\\" and groups adjacent steers under one header.\\n  - Reasoning passages record first-delta and close timestamps.\\n- **Builds on:** Existing cancellation policy and goal and loop machinery. It cites no named docs or issues.\\n- **Open or deferred:** It states no open questions or deferrals. It says only that configured iteration limits still apply.\\n- **Supersession:** None stated. It relates to doc 2's busy-boundary and live-feedback delivery.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Topic group C: Turn transcript and streaming\\n\\n### 6. `turn-transcript.md`\\n- **Status and date:**\\n  - \\\"Accepted design.\\\"\\n  - PR1 merged (`d4159db`) and PR2 merged (`46283cd`).\\n  - PR3 implemented on `feat/767-turn-transcript-pr3`.\\n  - The origin is a synthesis of three competing designs judged 2026-07-01.\\n  - Line references were verified against `develop@a933728` and have since drifted.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - A single-writer append-only part ledger (`TurnTranscript`) is the sole producer of persisted parts and live events.\\n  - Finalize becomes a verbatim reader, so live and reload are two projections of one ledger.\\n  - A `FieldStream` exactly-once handle is added.\\n  - Parent echoes are tagged (`restates_part_id`), not suppressed.\\n  - Seven or more content-matching reconciliation mechanisms are deleted.\\n  - A property test of \\\"live == reload\\\" is added.\\n- **Builds on:**\\n  - Epic #767.\\n  - gact-tui #232 (protocol convergence).\\n  - Symptom issues #731, #732, #733, #736.\\n  - Phase 0 branches fix/756, fix/757 and fix/761.\\n  - Commits b1b25d2, 712f5aa, f7339b1 and 68c33a9.\\n  - #646/#648 and #714, named as follow-on work.\\n- **Open or deferred (§9 Risks and §10):**\\n  - Rebase collision with fix/756.\\n  - Cross-thread ordering and the publish-under-lock coupling to non-blocking `bus.publish`.\\n  - Alias-view aliasing during the PR1/PR2 window.\\n  - Parent-echo tag misses if the parent paraphrases.\\n  - A **residual #756 hole**: parts published before a finalize crash are never persisted. PR-4 is to persist them or emit a voiding event.\\n  - PR5's single-vocabulary switch is client-visible and ships only behind the #232 conformance suite and a gact-tui release gate.\\n  - The remaining #7",
  "truncated": true
}

