  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading-guide notes: 13 design docs\\n\\nAll files are under `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/`.\\n\\n**Coverage and limits**\\n- Shell was blocked (read-only), so I read with `fs_read_file` and `fs_search_text`.\\n- I read every file in full, but several long table cells in `mcp-client-obligations-2026-07-28.md` came back cut off mid-cell by tool display. These are F7, H3, H8, D1 and E11. I report only what was visible.\\n- I did not read any doc these files cite but are not in the list, for example `vllm-local-qualification-20260904.md`.\\n\\n## Group A: MCP v2 / unified client (read in this order)\\n\\n### 1. `mcp-v2-understanding-2026-08.md`\\n- **Date/status:** written 2026-08-29. Companion to the obligations table for iowarp/clio-agent#1274.\\n- **Decided:** this is an explanation, not a decision record. Its thesis is that MCP v2 is stateless.\\n  - Every request carries its own `_meta`.\\n  - State becomes explicit handles: task id, subscription id, `requestState`.\\n  - Server-to-client interaction is inverted into MRTR (multi round-trip requests).\\n  - Capabilities are negotiated through a generic extensions framework.\\n  - Cache freshness is server-governed.\\n  - Refusals are typed and self-describing (-32020/-32021/-32022).\\n  - Hosts owe the human real consent surfaces.\\n- **Builds on:** the 2026-07-28 spec and the SEPs it cites. It names SEP-2577 for the deprecation of sampling, roots and logging. Companion: `mcp-client-obligations-2026-07-28.md`.\\n- **Open:** none stated. It is a conceptual summary only.\\n\\n### 2. `mcp-client-obligations-2026-07-28.md`\\n- **Date/status:** research record, 2026-08-29, later updated for the #1285 C1-S5 b1→b5 bump.\\n- **Decided:** a per-item obligations table (A1–J3) classifying each client duty as library-covered, \\\"OURS\\\", or done. Stated results:\\n  - Done: x-mcp-header retry (B3), listChanged invalidation wired into production (D2), CIMD deployment doc (H6).\\n  - Opt-in and default OFF: the response cache (E11). Its MUST-NOTs are \\\"structural by construction, not independently tested\\\".\\n  - Verified SDK gap: H3. The SDK always sends S256 and never checks `code_challenge_methods_supported`; the refusal is not implemented and was called out of scope.\\n  - Owner-ruled: the `createMessage` sampling primitive stays un-added (F7). C1-S7 (#1309) delivers the residual semantics via agent-driven elicitation.\\n  - Roots, sampling, logging and ping are only pinned zero-hit and era-gated.\\n- **Builds on:** #1274, #1285 (C1-S5), #1309. Test files named include `test_mcp_listen.py`, `test_mcp_adversarial.py`, `test_mcp_era_gated_removals.py` and `test_mcp_verification_probe_shortlist.py`.\\n- **Open (explicit, lines ~77–88):** B2 Base64 sentinel encoding; D1 `resources/updated`; E6 legacy -32002 acceptance; F2 enums/defaults; F8 per-request logLevel replacement; H2 AS-metadata discovery order and issuer check. H8's caveat is that `DurableFileTokenStorage` is keyed by `server_url`, not by AS issuer. J1–J3 (client-credentials, enterprise-managed auth, skills over MCP) are \\\"watch / only if demanded\\\".\\n\\n### 3. `mcp-2026-07-28-compat-matrix.md`\\n- **Date/status:** no date given. It reflects `fastmcp==4.0.0b5` (bumped from b1 under #1285 C1-S5 item 5).\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Pins: `fastmcp` and `fastmcp-tasks` 4.0.0b5, `mcp` 2.0.0, `fastapi>=0.140`, `pydantic>=2.12,<2.14`, `dspy==3.3.0b1`.\\n  - Migration: `as_proxy` becomes `create_proxy(transport)`, so the backend leg mirrors the front's protocol era. `mount(prefix=)` becomes `namespace=`.\\n  - Legacy compatibility spike: all four client/server pairings of FastMCP 4.0.0b1 and 3.2.4 pass, and a new client downgrades gracefully to 2025-11-25.\\n  - Owner decision (#1107): a `[tool.uv] override-dependencies = [\\\"mcp>=2.0.0\\\"]` entry neutralizes claude-agent-sdk's `mcp<2` bound, because CLIO uses the SDK only as an LLM provider.\\n- **Builds on:** #1285, #1106 (execution-handler slot), #1107.\\n- **Open:** the live SDK-session smoke \\\"runs at the P0 phase gate\\\". The override is to be dropped when upstream ships mcp-2 support. The default `memory://` docket is only for single-process dev; distributed tasks need Redis/Valkey plus a worker.\\n- **Note:** the matrix's spike evidence was on b1 (it says everything was verified green on b1 first).\\n\\n### 4. `mcp-client-unification-2026-08.md`\\n- **Date/status:** ACTIVE. Branch `feat/mcp-client-unification` was cut 2026-09-01. The status block is dated 2026-09-02. The C1-S7 re-scope is 2026-09-03. Umbrella is #1274 (+#1275).\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - One negotiated client for every server (letters a–f).\\n  - Reorientation (2026-09-01): campaign 1 builds the proper client and proves it against v1 servers, v2 servers and a synthetic exerciser. The relay path stays untouched. Relay removal moves to a separate campaign 2, together with letters (b)/(c) and the v1.7.0 release.\\n  - Defect: the proxy pins `_auto_internal_extensions = False`, which suppresses tasks and gives -32021 on `task=required` servers.\\n  - Probe verdict: in the modern era the task key is `server_capabilities.extensions`; in the legacy era it is per-tool `execution.taskSupport`.\\n  - Wait semantics: only typed refusals fail fast; slowness is never a verdict; progress resets the clock.\\n  - Relay inventory: ~58% dissolves into generic code, ~27% is legitimately transport-specific, ~15% is to be deleted.\\n  - Slice status: C1-S0, C1-S1 and C1-S2 are merged. C1-S3 (#1283), C1-S4 (#1284) and C1-S5 are described as landed or covered.\\n  - C1-S7 (#1309) is a campaign gate: agent-driven elicitation with a \\\"semantic firewall\\\" (not sampling, human fallback, url-mode excluded).\\n- **Builds on:** `mcp-v2-understanding-2026-08.md`, `mcp-client-obligations-2026-07-28.md`, #1274, #1275, #1119, #1255, #1278, #1280–#1284, #1286, #1309, #1310.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - The Apps-host revision alignment (`gact/mcp_apps.py` at 2026-01-26) is \\\"STILL OPEN\\\", deliberately untouched, and left to a future slice.\\n  - C1-S6 acceptance and landing have not happened.\\n  - Full live verification was prepared and \\\"runs on owner go-ahead\\\".\\n  - Campaign 2 will be re-planned at its own kickoff.\\n  - The doc says develop is \\\"already on 4.0.0b1; upstream b5\\\". Later docs say b5, so that line is stale.\\n  - The file ends in a slice and campaign-2 list, with no stated final outcome for campaign 1.\\n- **Supersession:** the Reorientation section explicitly supersedes the 2026-08-31 execution order.\\n\\n### 5. `mcp-fleet-memory-2026-07.md`\\n- **Date/status:** LANDED S1–S5, 2026-07-15; document date 2026-07-14. Issue #929, umbrella #930.\\n- **Decided:** make memory O(1) servers for N sessions. Slice table:\\n\\n  | Slice | Issue | PR |\\n  |---|---|---|\\n  | S1 | #931 | #937 |\\n  | S2 | #932 | #938 |\\n  | S3 | #933 | #939 |\\n  | S4 | #934 | #940 |\\n  | S5 | #935 | close-out PR |\\n\\n  Measured trajectory: 3.57 GB peak/final, down to 1.42 GB cold peak and 0.72 GB settled, against targets of ≤1.8 and ≤1.3 GB. The budget gate is wired into release checks.\\n- **Preserved semantics:** cwd pinning with `CLIO_KIT_ARTIFACTS`, per-workspace isolation, `UV_CACHE_DIR` isolation, and the #900 reaping invariant.\\n- **Builds on:** #921 (acceptance load), #702 (boot double-spawn), #867 (drain-lock pattern), #900, and upstream ask iowarp/clio-kit#296.\\n- **Open:** the \\\"Stretch\\\" item, shared-process fleets for absolute-path-only namespaces, is gated and not attempted. It is blocked while plot/geo/ndp would mix workspaces.\\n- **Note:** this is an earlier, separate campaign from the MCP v2 unification, but it concerns the same MCP fleet.\\n\\n## Group B: Shared runtime, provenance and provider routing (#1319–#1323)\\n\\n### 6. `hpc-mcp-runtime-semantics-1321.md`\\n- **Date/status:** handoff for the #1319–#1323 campaign. It says \\\"implemented, qualified locally, reviewed, committed on campaign branches\\\", and that the paired Agent and Kit packages are unreleased. No date inside.\\n- **Decided:** this is the umbrella summary.\\n  - #1319/#1321: one persistent `clio-kit[science]` install serves four separate MCP processes.\\n  - #1320: external-input provenance.\\n  - #1322/#1323: provider routing and output caps.\\n  - Local vLLM qualification on WSL2 CPU.\\n  - Evidence counts: Kit root gate 185 tests, 118 packages, integration 1 test in 68.49 s, routing gates 150+33+2, repair follow-up 30+3 and 4.\\n- **Builds on:** `shared-mcp-runtime-integration-1319.md`, `external-input-provenance-1320.md`, `provider-runtime-routing-1322-1323.md`, `vllm-local-qualification-20260904.md` (not read), and the Kit qualification report on GitHub.\\n- **Open:** the released installer still installs CLIO Kit 2.10.6 (legacy runtime semantics) until the paired release. The local vLLM run does not qualify AMD GPU, drivers, containers, HPC filesystem or performance. The original live Granite-to-Qwen leak was not reproduced. \\\"Historical partial rounds in earlier reports remain negative or superseded evidence.\\\"\\n- **Supersession:** it says earlier partial rounds are superseded by its final gates.\\n\\n### 7. `shared-mcp-runtime-integration-1319.md`\\n- **Date/status:** none stated. It is an operator guide.\\n- **Decided:** one `clio-kit[science]` tool install serves NDP, Geo, Pandas and Plot. Each declaration stays `clio-kit mcp-server NAME`. Normal discovery does not solve, build, hash or gc. Installers default to the legacy `clio-kit==2.10.6` and accept `CLIO_KIT_PACKAGE` as a candidate override. `scripts/qualify_shared_mcp_runtime.py` provides bounded local qualification. Upgrades are package-manager operations done after stopping servers.\\n- **Builds on:** the paired Kit release. No other docs are cited.\\n- **Open:** the pin \\\"predates this contract\\\" until the paired release exists. It does not claim release publication, HPC filesystem timings, allocated-byte savings or live vLLM qualification.\\n\\n### 8. `external-input-provenance-1320.md`\\n- **Date/status:** backend capture is implemented and gated. The UI half was re-landed under #1336. No date inside.\\n- **Decided:** successful calls to the built-in filesystem reader and CLIO Kit Geo/Pandas/Plot record durable `used` edges (locator, basename, schema arg, evidence `external_input_not_hashed`) without opening, hashing or copying the source. Unknown contracts get an `external_input_contract_unknown` warning rather than a fabricated edge. Recording failures never change the tool result. UI is delivered as presenter blocks in `tool_result.presentation.blocks`, so no client change was needed.\\n- **Builds on:** #1320, #1336, gact-tui #389 (which replaced the old `apps/web` client), and `test_hpc_external_inputs.py` and `test_artifacts_s5.py`.\\n- **Open:** \\\"No full Agent suite, live HPC measurement, or installed end-to-end CLIO qualification is claimed.\\\" The browser gate is a component/API-fixture test, not a full-stack run.\\n- **Supersession:** the original UI implementation (`codex/provider-runtime-provenance` gact-tui commit `d395796e`, written against the legacy `apps/web`) is superseded and its branch is gone. Its Chromium/pnpm verification steps no longer apply.\\n\\n### 9. `provider-runtime-routing-1322-1323.md`\\n- **Date/status:** none stated.\\n- **Decided:** summarization inference resolves from the owning LM.\\n  - A model-only override keeps the caller's provider settings.\\n  - A provider override keeps only provider-independent sampling.\\n  - The `summarizer.*` fields are configurable, with empty/null inheriting, zero omitting the output cap, positive sent exactly, and negative invalid.\\n  - No response classification, repair or synthesis.\\n  - `finish_reason=length` raises `LMOutputTruncatedError` after history and usage are recorded.\\n  - It includes a call-site audit table.\\n- **Builds on:** `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md` (for env aliases); no earlier design docs are named.\\n- **Open:** \\\"Broad matrix validation remains CI-owned.\\\"\\n\\n### 10. `unified-spotter-provenance-mcp-2026-08.md`\\n- **Date/status:** \\\"implemented an",
