  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading-guide notes: six design docs\\n\\nAll files are in `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/`. Shell was blocked (read-only session), and `fs_read_file` and `fs_search_text` return only about 12,000 characters per call. I read through line-anchored searches.\\n\\n**Coverage gaps**\\n- **`react-loop-completion-2026-09.md`, `model-stream-recovery.md`:** read in full.\\n- **`composer-pipeline-landing-2026-09.md`:** read in full (292 lines).\\n- **`compaction-checkpoint-1339.md`:** read lines 1–434 in full.\\n- **`agent-loop-rebuild-2026-09.md` (1837 lines):** I did not read these ranges, and the summary below may miss open items in them:\\n  - roughly 981–1000\\n  - 1102–1118 (the rest of the History mode sub-plan)\\n  - 1326–1357 (the rest of Phase 11a and the start of 11b)\\n  - 1458–1512\\n  - 1614–1630\\n  - 1702–1756 (final-verification sections A and B)\\n- **`compaction-prompt-research-2026-10.md` (~948 lines):** I read lines 1–160 (Codex, Gemini), 748–948 (comparison, failure modes, recommendation, sources) and the section headings. I did not read §1.3's tail through §1.11 (Claude Code, OpenHands, Cline, Roo, Aider, Goose, LangChain, Letta, blogs) or the §2 table.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. `agent-loop-rebuild-2026-09.md`\\n\\n**Date / status:** APPROVED 2026-09-28 (owner). Line 3 says \\\"Phase 1 implemented\\\", but the body is updated through 2026-10-02. By then the implementation is complete on `rework_agent`, CI is green, and the release PRs to main (#1604, gact-tui#526) are open and not merged (line 1646).\\n\\n**Group:** Agent loop and context (core campaign).\\n\\n**Decided.**\\n- **Own the loop:** `ClioReAct(dspy.Module)` replaces the `ReActV2` subclass. Tools run concurrently, and cancel is checked at every boundary.\\n- **Context system:** clio-core is the single context store, with one event log and two projections (UI and agent). Context spans turns, and injections, steers and child results are recorded at the step boundary.\\n- **No silent repair:** deterministic fixes are recorded as `injection` parts and told to the model.\\n  - A path error becomes a \\\"did you mean\\\" hint.\\n  - The circuit breaker is configurable.\\n  - Oversize results spill to a file.\\n- **Providers:** DSPy 3.4 engines replace the LiteLLM/CustomLLM path. The Codex SDK was removed in Phase 10 (2026-10-01); Codex direct (WebSocket) is the only Codex path.\\n- **Extract:** DSPy's extract is config-driven.\\n- **Failure policy:**\\n  - A typed error is preferred over any fallback.\\n  - The only sanctioned fallback is a loud \\\"History mode\\\" when the clio-core binding is absent. `LocalFSStore` was deleted.\\n- **Other pieces:** session bring-up off the first message, the Phase 11a `ContextView`, visible and lossless compaction (11b), and BestOfN/Refine as runtime self-refinement (Phase 9).\\n\\n**Builds on.**\\n- `react-loop-completion-2026-09.md`, which it amends.\\n- `mcp-client-unification-2026-08.md`, for the relay campaign.\\n- #1237, which Phase 7 supersedes.\\n- #1339, whose staged-checkpoint \\\"F1\\\" design is superseded by Phase 11b.\\n- #1281, #905 and #1112 (clio-core).\\n- #1559, #1560 and #1577.\\n- DSPy 3.4.0 and its lm15 layer.\\n\\n**Open or deferred** (as stated):\\n- **Phase 9 edges:**\\n  - a new user message arrives instead of a pick;\\n  - the drafts question is cancelled or expires.\\n- **Counting rule:** whether \\\"deletions ≥ additions\\\" is counted over `src` or the whole branch is left to the owner. `src` meets it (+14,884/−16,082) and the whole branch does not.\\n- **clio-schemas:** `injection` and `notice` are in 0.5.2 (#18), not yet released. `agent_message`, `context_reference`, `mcp_app` and `resource` blocks are emitted but not modelled.\\n- **gact-tui e2e:** the Linux baseline for `summarization-row-collapsed.png` is missing.\\n- **Context view:** BM25 search is unavailable on clio-core 2.2.1 (#905). The session index grows O(chunks), and archiving pre-anchor entries is deferred over a data-loss risk.\\n- **Transcript file:** turning `transcript.file` off needs an atomic replace. This was later done in #1578, but this is recorded as \\\"not needed for release\\\".\\n- **Compaction:** the compaction issue (#1559, #1560) is deferred by the owner.\\n- **Relay onto MCP tasks:** a separate follow-on campaign (owner, 2026-09-30).\\n- **DSPy upstream issue:** posting the lazy-`anyio` issue to stanfordnlp/dspy awaits the owner's OK.\\n- **Release gates:** the Chrome UI check and the 1k/10k benchmark are owner-run release gates.\\n- **Release order and leftovers (line 1651–1652):** the merge order is set. Still left for the owner are filing the clio-core `PutBlob` issue and a DSPy stream-reset proposal for drops after visible output. The unfinished branch `fix/transcript-replace-lean-atoms` is untested.\\n\\n**Supersession:**\\n- It amends `react-loop-completion-2026-09.md` (the 2026-09-30 amendment).\\n- Its Phase 3 `LocalFSStore` fallback is superseded by the History mode sub-plan (2026-10-01).\\n- Phase 11b supersedes the `#1339` staged-checkpoint behaviour (line 1004).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. `react-loop-completion-2026-09.md`\\n\\n**Date / status:** accepted 2026-09-05. Amended 2026-09-30 by the agent-loop rebuild, phase 6.\\n\\n**Group:** Agent loop and context.\\n\\n**Decided.** The model owns action selection in the ReAct loop, and CLIO never calls the model again after the loop returns. A response with no tool call is a normal direct response, returned as `answer` with `termination_reason=\\\"direct_response\\\"`. A valid model-selected `submit` stays available. Parse failures and iteration-cap exhaustion stop without a forced submit.\\n\\nSeven recovery mechanisms were removed: empty-tool-call retries, the post-loop forced submit, submit repair over History, schema-repair resampling, adapter tool-intent recovery, answer synthesis from observations, and empty-answer classification. The rationale given is that this is a responsibility boundary, so stronger models are not forced through recovery built for weaker ones.\\n\\n**Amendment (2026-09-30).** DSPy's own `ChainOfThought` extract may run once, under these conditions:\\n- `agents.react_extract.enabled` is on (default true).\\n- The loop took more than `after_steps` model steps (default 3).\\n- The loop ended by `max_iters`, or by a direct response on a signature whose declared outputs were not produced.\\n\\nIt fills only the missing outputs and never replaces the user-visible answer. `submit`, `ask_user`/`plan_exit` yields, `context_window_exceeded`, plain `question -> answer` and short loops never extract. `enabled: false` restores the original contract.\\n\\n**Builds on:** the 2026-09-05 decision supersedes the earlier landing decision recorded in `composer-pipeline-landing-2026-09.md`. The amendment cites the agent-loop rebuild doc.\\n\\n**Open:** none stated.\\n\\n**Supersession:** it supersedes the \\\"ground-rule violations dropped\\\" rationale in the composer landing doc, and it is itself narrowed by the 2026-09-30 amendment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. `model-stream-recovery.md`\\n\\n**Date / status:** none stated.\\n\\n**Group:** Provider and transport resilience (loop-adjacent).\\n\\n**Decided.** A \\\"connection closed mid-chunk\\\" error proves only an interrupted transport, not its cause. The doc names gateway idle timeout, upstream failure, proxy or network disconnect as indistinguishable without gateway logs. A UI heartbeat does not keep the gateway connection alive.\\n\\nDSPy retries typed transient failures only before any stream chunk is forwarded. CLIO adds narrower recovery for stateless OpenAI-compatible chat requests that propose only local function tools:\\n- **Before public answer text:** restart the generation. Completed tool calls are not re-executed. Interrupted reasoning stays in the transcript, closed by a service notice. Partial reasoning and incomplete tool proposals are discarded.\\n- **Backoff and budget:** 1s, 2s, then capped at 8s, bounded by `limits.lm_transient_retries` / `CLIO_LM_TRANSIENT_RETRIES` (default 2; 0 disables).\\n- **After public answer text:** report a clear provider error and keep the partial transcript, with no silent restart.\\n- **Out of scope:** stateful SDK engines, provider-native tools, and auth, config, policy or arbitrary tool failures keep their own paths.\\n\\n**Builds on:** no earlier docs or issues are cited.\\n\\n**Open:** it says the local qualification does not establish MAG's production timeout and does not exercise inference on the protected Argonne computer. Nothing else is stated.\\n\\n**Supersession:** none stated. The agent-loop rebuild (Phase 4 progress) separately records WebSocket-1012 reconnect-before-output, and later #1600 and #1602 for Codex.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. `composer-pipeline-landing-2026-09.md`\\n\\n**Date / status:** \\\"LANDING\\\" (no calendar date). Fix slices A1–A4 are complete on `codex/clio-composer-pipeline`, PR #1278 → develop. Its verification block shows 6516 passed, 0 failed. CI on #1278 is the merge gate.\\n\\n**Group:** Composer, resources and campaign landings.\\n\\n**Decided.**\\n- **Rebuild, not merge:** Codex's five-repo composer wave was not mergeable as-is. The clio-agent branch was reviewed at `7bd46c95` as a 163-commit-stale fork. It was rebuilt on develop in three `port:` commits (resources, message intents, provider catalog) plus fix slices, with develop winning wholesale on overlap.\\n- **Dropped:**\\n  - the codex app-server/cancel/pool lane, because develop's sdk-native refactor (`ce09130e`) deleted that transport;\\n  - four ground-rule violations (`_frame_codex_answer`, `_direct_response_outputs`, `capability_contract.py`, and the `_builtin_agents() -> []` deletion);\\n  - the `_SECTION` de-anchoring in `runtime/lm_stream.py`, where develop's file wins.\\n- **Fixed with failing-first tests:** six semantic defects, plus unbounded intent-store growth and about 35 hardcoded tunables moved to `conf.resolve`.\\n- **Marketplace:** the default blueprint moves to `base-agent` (marketplace PR #58 merged). Develop's builtin `main` stays as the offline fallback.\\n- **Correction:** the wave is mostly backend, not UI.\\n\\n**Builds on:** #1278, #1290, #1291, #1273, #737 (event-sourcing consolidation), RULE 2 and RULE 4, `system-cleanup-2026-07.md`, clio-schemas 0.2.3, and `docs/design/research/clio-composer-attachments/report-source.md`. gact-tui #382, marketplace #58/#59 and clio-web-search #4 are the sibling-repo PRs.\\n\\n**Open** (§(d) and §(e)):\\n- **RULE 4 deviation:** three new persistent stores must be folded into the #737 normalized log when it lands.\\n- **Schema gap:** `ResourceMessageBlock` pends clio-schemas 0.2.4, and the client uses a tolerant hand schema meanwhile.\\n- **Dropped Codex capabilities:** native image inputs, the turn/interrupt handshake and stderr diagnostics are gaps to re-land on the sdk-native path.\\n- **Catalog staleness:** `provider_catalog.refreshed` fires only on explicit refresh, so there is no stale-catalog push.\\n- **EarthScope pack:** de-handcuffing is unfinished, and its prompt-assertion tests will need to move with it.\\n- **`MessageBehavior`:** `reasoning_effort`, `execution_mode` and `confirmation_policy` have no server consumer.\\n- **Flaky test:** `test_mcp_fleet_lifecycle.py::test_boot_listing_is_sequential_one_chain_at_a_time` failed in 1 of 3 runs. It is untouched by this branch and not patched.\\n- **Sibling PRs:** gact-tui #382 and clio-web-search #4 remain open.\\n\\n**Supersession:** a blockquote (lines ~76–80) says the ReAct \\\"drop `_direct_response_outputs`\\\" decision was superseded on 2026-09-05 by `react-loop-completion-2026-09.md`. The Scrollspy recommendation in the attachments research report is superseded; the report is deliberately not edited.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. `compaction-checkpoint-1339.md`\\n\\n**Date / status:** landed on `fix/1339-compaction-checkpoint` (HEAD `4b8427f3`, four commits above `0d0e3e2b`), \\\"not yet merged\\\". No calendar date is stated. The live-leg evidence directories are timestamped 2026-09-11.\\n\\n**Group:** Compaction and context.\\n\\n**Decided.**\\n- **Checkpoint",
