  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading guide notes: 9 design docs\\n\\nAll paths are under `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/`. `shell_bash` was refused (read-only session), so I read with `fs_read_file` and `fs_search_text`.\\n\\n**Coverage limits**\\n- Fully read: `artifact-provenance-design.md`, `artifacts-campaign-2026-07.md`, `artifacts-research-2026-07.md`, `document-artifacts-human-review-2026-07.md`, `a2ui-release-handoff-2026-10-03.md`, `widget-visual-feedback.md`, `response-feedback.md`.\\n- `provenance-adapters-and-artifact-storage-2026-08.md` (74 KB, about 1,370 lines) was only partly read. I read the header and §1–3.3, the heading list, §9 (decision ledger), the start of §10, §12–13, §14.1–14.3 (start) and the start of §14.x. I did not read §3.4–8, the rest of §10, §11 beyond 11.3–11.6, or the tail of §14.3.\\n- `a2ui-compat-campaign-2026-09.md` (46 KB) was read except the slice-ledger table rows (S2–S9), which the tool cut off mid-cell, and the text between \\\"Live evidence\\\" and the per-agent follow-up.\\n\\n## Group A: Artifacts and provenance (2026-07 → 08)\\n\\n### 1. `artifacts-research-2026-07.md` (prior-art survey)\\n- **Decided:** Nothing; it describes itself as \\\"a survey, not a design\\\". Its §5 lists \\\"directions, not a plan\\\":\\n  - register at the output-path grounding hook (`execution.py:1176`);\\n  - adopt clio-relay's `ArtifactRef` shape;\\n  - use W&B version semantics;\\n  - treat UI payloads and transform specs as artifact kinds;\\n  - use A2A parts for delivery;\\n  - keep records as a projection over existing stores (RULE 4 / #737).\\n- **Builds on:** The owner framing (`b = transform(a)`); a survey of Claude, other agent products, A2A/MCP, W&B, DVC, OpenLineage, PROV, RO-Crate and Pachyderm; clio-relay issue #58 and PR #59 (`ArtifactUse`, content-pinned used edges); #948.\\n- **Open:** No explicit open-items section. Its stated verdict is that clio-agent has no artifact record today and no agent product ships this model.\\n- **Status:** Dated 2026-07. §4b says the Cowork capture design is \\\"Superseded by `docs/design/artifact-provenance-design.md` (v2, 2026-07-16)\\\".\\n- **Group:** Artifacts and provenance (research input).\\n\\n### 2. `artifact-provenance-design.md` (v2)\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Scope is two campaigns: A (artifacts plus provenance floor) and B (sandboxing plus provenance upgrade).\\n  - The model is never in the chain of custody; artifacts are designated, not discovered.\\n  - Content hash is identity (W&B-style versions).\\n  - Identity evidence is classed (`hashed-at-use`, `authority-asserted`, `stat-pinned`).\\n  - Custody is tiered (`isolated`, `app-private`, `referenced`).\\n  - Transform records carry a tiered `environment` field.\\n  - Capture uses mechanisms plus per-edge evidence, not a single ladder.\\n  - Attribution is lease-scoped, so overlap produces `contended` records.\\n  - Tracing is demoted.\\n  - The inert `structured_outputs.artifacts` field is deleted and replaced by a `create_artifact` tool.\\n- **Builds on:** The earlier Cowork design (same filename, v1) after an adversarial review (six criticisms resolved in §1); `artifacts-research-2026-07.md`; #948/#951 (leases), #933, #949, #930, #737, relay #59.\\n- **Open (§6):**\\n  1. Acceptance policy for agent-proposed designations (over-designation risk).\\n  2. CAS budget defaults and GC cadence.\\n  3. Timing of relay schema convergence for mechanism/edge-evidence fields.\\n  4. Whether Campaign B's container mode is repro-substrate-only or also revives tracing.\\n- **Status:** \\\"design notes, 2026-07-16\\\".\\n- **Group:** Artifacts and provenance (authority design). It supersedes the Cowork v1 design (per the research doc §4b).\\n\\n### 3. `artifacts-campaign-2026-07.md` (landed record)\\n- **Decided:** Records Campaign A as landed in slices S1–S7 (#967–#973):\\n  - registry projection;\\n  - wire identity and routes;\\n  - `create_artifact`;\\n  - version chains;\\n  - TransformRecords;\\n  - CAS and GC;\\n  - S7 (RO-Crate export with `reproduce.py`, grounding and graders re-sourced to the registry, prose migration, CI guard).\\n  - Path-string scrapers were deleted.\\n  - Grounding deliberately keeps a schema-derived extension vocabulary (a recorded hybrid).\\n- **Builds on:** The design doc and research doc (named as \\\"authority docs\\\"); parent issue #966; clio-core#793.\\n- **Open (\\\"Scope held for later campaigns\\\" and \\\"Typed follow-ups\\\"):**\\n  - Campaign B and the `isolated` custody class;\\n  - gact-tui client rendering (artifacts panel / Recreate tab);\\n  - mcpui/a2ui rendering;\\n  - federation transport;\\n  - the AGENTIC replay runner;\\n  - the `plan`-kind producer;\\n  - relay convergence for `ArtifactUse` (frozen `extra='forbid'`).\\n- **Status:** 2026-07, close-out of the campaign. It is the implemented counterpart of docs 1–2.\\n- **Group:** Artifacts and provenance.\\n\\n### 4. `document-artifacts-human-review-2026-07.md`\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Documents are format-aware views over the immutable artifact registry, and the native file stays canonical.\\n  - A highlight-to-comment flow creates an `artifact_review` part bound to artifact ID, version, SHA-256 and anchor, and continues the session.\\n  - Only native comments starting with `@clio` are agent instructions.\\n  - ONLYOFFICE and Collabora are optional embedded editors.\\n  - Static HTML is sandboxed; executable HTML goes to Live Web.\\n  - Package-inventory guard: editing blocks rather than dropping unknown parts.\\n- **Builds on:** The artifact registry and versioning (docs 2–3); Live Web, A2UI and MCP Apps are named as separate paths. It cites no issue numbers.\\n- **Open:** Real ONLYOFFICE/Collabora container acceptance is \\\"separate\\\" and must not be claimed unless run. Round-tripping of third-party extensions is not guaranteed. Missing editors or converters are an explicit unavailable state.\\n- **Status:** No date or status line in the file (the filename says 2026-07).\\n- **Group:** Artifacts and provenance (document layer).\\n\\n### 5. `provenance-adapters-and-artifact-storage-2026-08.md` (partly read; see limits)\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - The ARC semantic-event highway is the parent \\\"agentic provenance stream\\\".\\n  - Artifact provenance is an overlapping substream selected from it, with no duplicate emission.\\n  - Agentic providers are JSONL (default), a CLIO pool and Flowcept; artifact providers are native (`file`/`clio_core`) and CMF, each with provider-scoped storage.\\n  - CMF and Flowcept are optional lazy-import dependencies.\\n  - CLIO owns version history and SHA-256 identity; provider-native hashes go in storage receipts.\\n  - Section 9 lists accepted and rejected items.\\n  - Implemented: JSONL and Flowcept agentic providers, native and CMF artifact providers (reference and local DVC custody), live-verified on `homelab` (§14).\\n- **Builds on:** ARC (`arc/memory.py`), `semantic_events.py`, the artifact-provenance design, the campaign record and `docs/design/unified-arc-highway.md` (§13.1). It cites external CMF, Flowcept and IOWarp Core commits. It points to `unified-spotter-provenance-mcp-2026-08.md` for the query plane, which I did not open.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - §9.3 Deferred:\\n    - importing external CMF lineage;\\n    - a CMF team server;\\n    - remote CMF/MinIO stores;\\n    - CTE as sole archive;\\n    - queue/spool overflow policy;\\n    - receipt persistence and recursion guard;\\n    - the large-file async identity event schema;\\n    - whether multiple non-JSONL agentic providers are allowed by default.\\n  - §12: eleven questions for the HPE CMF team (`/mlmd_push` contract, side-effect-free writer, Python 3.12, hash labelling and so on).\\n  - §14: the native `clio_core` store, CMF remotes and a Windows-native MLMD runtime remain unqualified.\\n- **Status:** Header says \\\"implemented… end-to-end live qualification recorded\\\", dated 2026-08-21. §14 records live runs on 2026-08-22 and 2026-08-26 (the 08-26 run closes the earlier zero-edges result).\\n- **Group:** Artifacts and provenance (provider layer). It extends docs 2–3 and its query-plane note is corrected by the Spotter doc.\\n\\n## Group B: A2UI (2026-09 → 10)\\n\\n### 6. `a2ui-compat-campaign-2026-09.md`\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - CLIO becomes a truthful A2UI 0.9.1 agent and renderer.\\n  - Catalogs are blueprint-declared and pack-shipped like MCP servers, with a `catalog.clio.json` sidecar.\\n  - Official shapes are used verbatim; validation uses the official JSON Schema at runtime.\\n  - Durable actions are an `a2ui_action` transcript part.\\n  - All events go to the agent unless the sidecar declares otherwise.\\n  - Capability advertisement lives once in `packages/core`.\\n  - clio-schemas goes to 0.3.0.\\n  - Slices S0–S9 are listed in a ledger.\\n  - Every red-baseline gap was closed at S9 (2026-09-17).\\n  - A bounded public claim is stated.\\n  - A follow-up makes `a2ui_catalogs` a complete per-agent allowlist (v15 S8, 0.9.4.17).\\n- **Builds on:** Umbrella #1363 (also #1374); the A2UI spec pinned at commit `0086493c…`; a claim-by-claim validation of the earlier Codex proposal; clio-schemas, gact-tui and marketplace PRs (#412, #411, #11, #69, #70).\\n- **Open:**\\n  - Not supported: A2UI 1.0 (only seams are kept), inline catalogs, A2A transport, pack-shipped renderer code.\\n  - The waiting-user live cell is model-dependent and not observed live.\\n  - Intermittent Windows clio-core daemon crashes are tracked on #1242 and affected the live re-run.\\n  - Marketplace PR #70 was not yet mergeable at the time of writing.\\n  - The 0.11.x library upgrade is its own slice.\\n  - The S0 row still reads \\\"in progress\\\" and the S6 status cell is blank in the ledger, although the closure section says all gaps closed.\\n- **Status:** \\\"ACTIVE — approved 2026-09-16\\\", with closure notes dated 2026-09-17 and a later follow-up. It supersedes `external/gact-tui/docs/review/a2ui-v091-compatibility-campaign-2026-08-30.md` (not in this set).\\n- **Group:** A2UI.\\n\\n### 7. `a2ui-release-handoff-2026-10-03.md`\\n- **Decided:** Not a design; a publication handoff. It says to integrate the combined `a2ui_fixes` branches (not older slices separately), lists four repos with merge targets and published heads, and gives a release sequence (schemas, then agent dependency and mirrors, then marketplace, then UI and agent).\\n- **Builds on:** The A2UI work, widget gallery and demo work of this campaign. It cites no issue numbers.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - Version metadata is stale: the schemas branch declares 0.5.2, which is already published; the agent pins `clio-schemas==0.5.1` and declares 0.9.4.24.\\n  - Branch divergence counts are a snapshot and must be refreshed.\\n  - The third linked Abaqus example is blocked because the real mesh/density cycle exports are missing (CHPC SSH authentication was rejected).\\n  - Crash recovery and damaged ARC state need release qualification.\\n  - Raw recordings are only locally preserved.\\n  - No merge, tag or release was performed, and no full release gates were run.\\n- **Status:** Prepared 2026-10-03; \\\"not a release qualification report\\\".\\n- **Group:** A2UI. It follows doc 6 and likely feeds doc 8.\\n\\n### 8. `widget-visual-feedback.md`\\n- **Decided:** Accepted design (expanded after the 2026-10-08 review) for a general loop: inspect, control, render, screenshot, reason, adjust.\\n  - Schema-derived control manifests.\\n  - Bounded `capture_a2ui_surface`: one viewer, up to 20 s, images up to 5 MB and 4096 px; never returns a stale frame.\\n  - Annotations with explicit coordinate frames.\\n  - Saved dashboards remain immutable artifact versions.\\n  - `review-visual-presentation` holds the procedures.\\n- **Builds on:** The pending dashboard/question stack (`inspect_a2ui_surface`, `update_a2ui_components`, `update_a2ui_data_model`), existing image semantics, and `../verification/widget-visual-feedback-2026-10-09.md` (not in this set, not read).\\n- **Open:**\\n  - VIGIL integration is explicitly deferred.\\n  - No headless viewer is implemented.\\n  - A generic cross-component overlay is a separate catalog exten",
