  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading-guide findings: design docs in `design/`\\n\\nAll nine files were read. The three large ones (`codex-rework-landing`, `governance-surfaces`, `system-cleanup`) were read partly through truncated results and partly through line-context searches. I saw every line range, but several very long bullets in the landing doc were cut off at about 500 characters in search output. These are the Phase 1, 2, 4 and 5 records and the qualification bullets. Those bullets are not quoted in full, and no claim below depends on their cut-off tails.\\n\\nAll paths are under `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/`.\\n\\n## Topic group A: OS sandboxing (a chain: campaign → rework → net)\\n\\n### 1. `sandboxing-campaign-2026-07.md`\\n- **Status:** \\\"the landed record\\\" for umbrella #974, July 2026. The file does not state a final status for the live gates.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Campaign B (B1–B6, issues #975–#980) built OS write-confinement.\\n  - It used a backend ladder of srt, then Landlock, then none, with srt as the Windows path.\\n  - It added a CONNECT-only network chokepoint that allows and records egress by default.\\n  - Grants became recorded `boundary.*` events.\\n  - Provenance was upgraded: `gap` became `policy_violation`, `lease-window` became `fence_proven`, and egress became `used web:<domain>@<time>`.\\n  - `file_policy` stays as an advisory twin.\\n  - It includes a `sandbox_conformance` sweep for zero untyped degrades.\\n- **Builds on:** #966 (artifacts) and `docs/design/artifact-provenance-design.md` §5.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - The five campaign-done live gates still show \\\"pending\\\" placeholders (`<!-- LIVE-GATE-n RESULT -->`).\\n  - Only the unit matrix for gate 4 is marked green.\\n  - Native Windows restricted-token implementation is explicitly \\\"not built\\\" and listed as a future rung.\\n- **Superseded:** its srt-based design is replaced by file 2, which deletes srt. The live-gate placeholders are not updated in this file.\\n\\n### 2. `codex-sandbox-rework-2026-07.md`\\n- **Status:** July 2026. The deletion inventory is marked DONE (B-codex-5, 2026-07-23).\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Replace srt with the OpenAI Codex sandbox (v0.145.0) as the sole OS-fence backend on all platforms.\\n  - srt's native-Windows leg failed to enforce: `srt-win wfp verify` failed with 0x80070005, and issue srt #402 reports writes escaping `allowWrite`.\\n  - The verified invocation recipe is a `-p` profile layer file in the default `CODEX_HOME`. Custom `CODEX_HOME` and `-c` overrides were rejected.\\n  - Slices B-codex-1 to B-codex-5 are defined.\\n  - srt modules, reasons and tests are deleted.\\n- **Builds on:** #974 and the Campaign B ladder and seams (`wrap_confined`).\\n- **Left open:** the Network section is \\\"TBD in the net slice; the write-fence lands first\\\". Nothing else is stated as open.\\n- **Supersedes** `sandboxing-campaign-2026-07.md` for the backend choice.\\n\\n### 3. `codex-net-2026-07.md`\\n- **Status:** owner directive 2026-07-23. Fleet-under-codex was live-validated 2026-07-24.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - De-defer the network pillar that file 2 postponed. Part of \\\"observability and sandboxing has no value\\\" without egress recording, per the owner.\\n  - **Network policy:** reads are allowed and recorded. Writes are blockable and escalated for human permission.\\n  - **Recipe A:** the codex managed proxy chains to a clio upstream chokepoint. It was proven live on Windows.\\n  - The `net_enforcement` value `codex-net-deferred` becomes `proxy-enforced`.\\n  - Fleet fixes made automatic:\\n    - A: the child cache-env redirect.\\n    - B: Windows RX grants.\\n    - C: pre-provisioned MCP envs.\\n  - Slices N1–N3 are defined.\\n- **Builds on:**\\n  - `codex-sandbox-rework-2026-07.md`.\\n  - #974, #1024 (observed-domain path), B5's `set_egress_gate` and the step-0 floor at b5b6c7c0.\\n  - Codex issue codex#22387, a Linux DNS caveat.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - An HTTPS CONNECT tunnel is opaque, so write-detection is clean only for plain-HTTP verbs and host policy. This is documented as a limit.\\n  - The N1–N3 live gates on Windows plus Linux (WSL) are described as acceptance criteria. The file does not record their completion.\\n  - Linux still needs the cache redirect and pre-provisioned envs.\\n\\n## Topic group B: governance and live gate\\n\\n### 4. `governance-surfaces-2026-07.md`\\n- **Status:** \\\"FINAL\\\", baseline `develop @ be24b6ec` (v0.8.1, post-#1031). Campaign acceptance record dated 2026-07-28.\\n- **Decided:** one governance engine, with planning mode and hooks expressed as data on the #1031 `grant_resolver`.\\n  - **Engine (P0):**\\n    - Priority bands and most-restrictive-wins.\\n    - Real `mode` and `event` axes.\\n    - Annotation source of truth.\\n    - The engine merge is fenced to the tool, domain, `plan_acl` and hook kinds.\\n  - **Planning (P1):**\\n    - A skill privileged-effects substrate.\\n    - Declarative plan ACL rows.\\n    - Shell governed by the OS write-fence, not a parser.\\n    - A plan file under `.clio/plans`.\\n    - A durable `plan_exit` defer.\\n    - A `write_todos` tool.\\n    - `chat` mode deleted.\\n  - **Hooks (P2):**\\n    - Delete both old hook systems.\\n    - Rebuild one dispatcher on the `ToolRuntimeHooks` seam.\\n    - Subprocess exit-0/exit-2 wire.\\n    - BeforeModel via a `dspy.LM` wrapper.\\n    - Trust, introspection and audit.\\n  - **P4 goal evaluation:** LLM-judge only, with loop bounds as the hard stops.\\n- **Builds on:**\\n  - #1031 (`grant_resolver`, `deferred_resumes`), #1032, #1057 and #1074/#1075.\\n  - #948 (AgentTask projection pattern).\\n  - #646/#648 (`workflow_state`).\\n  - #966.\\n  - Companion docs `hooks-research-2026-07.md` and `planning-mode-research-2026-07.md`.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - The only postponed item is hardening the Windows shell fence from floor to hard. It is blocked on an external OS sandbox that is still in alpha. The file says the design then needs no change.\\n  - P2.6 cross-restart durability is a flagged RESIDUAL. The durable surface shipped, but rehydrating pending defers into `app.state.permissions` at startup is not wired, and deterministic replay-resume is a follow-up slice.\\n  - The accepted residual is that the judge is transcript-persuadable.\\n  - There is a tracked cross-repo sweep: the gact-tui `contract/SPEC.md` `x_clio_hook_backend` enum needs `declarative` added.\\n- **Related:** the Windows-floor caveat connects to the codex fence in group A.\\n\\n### 5. `live-gate-governance-1057-verdict.json`\\n- **Date:** the goal's `created_at` is 2026-07-29T09:26. The governance doc dates the acceptance record 2026-07-28, so the two dates differ by a day.\\n- **Verdict recorded:** `\\\"pass\\\": true`.\\n  - All 17 entries in `required_gates` are `true`: CTE/ARC live, hook discovered and fired, plan write blocked, plan-exit with no phantom approval, reserved-metadata rejected, cron registered and fired, loop armed and ended on a typed bound, goal armed and met, and zero degrade reasons.\\n  - Run details: model `sonnet`, core port 9423, the CTE listener process is `clio_run.exe`, and `loop_stop_reason` is `loop_budget`.\\n- **Builds on:** it is the output of `scripts/live_gate_governance_1057.py`, referenced in `governance-surfaces-2026-07.md`. The JSON itself cites no earlier docs.\\n- **Open items:** the JSON states none.\\n- **Discrepancy to flag:** `plan_denial_in_trace` is `false`. It is not among the required gates. The governance doc's acceptance paragraph lists \\\"plan write-deny + denial in trace\\\" among the passed items. A reader should know this gate was false in the verdict.\\n- **Not required, but true:** `loop_stop_reason_sticky`, `loop_rearm_denied_live` and `goal_no_predicate`.\\n\\n## Topic group C: campaigns and hygiene\\n\\n### 6. `system-cleanup-2026-07.md`\\n- **Status:** Phases 0–1 complete (2026-07-05). The execution section also records Phase 3 complete (2026-07-08) and Phase 4 code complete (2026-07-08), with \\\"owner-gated remainders only\\\". The header line (\\\"Phases 2–4 open\\\") is stale against that section.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - A master plan from a 2026-07-01 nine-reviewer audit.\\n  - Ground rules: grounding release first; spec follows reality; every degradation is loud; failing-first tests; delete, don't gate; no accretion.\\n  - Eight systemic diagnoses.\\n  - An issue map (clio #755–#774, #830, #841; gact-tui #224–#236).\\n  - Phases 0–4.\\n- **Builds on:** umbrellas clio #775 and gact-tui #237, the `gact-tui/contract/SPEC.md` drift and the #767 `TurnTranscript` work.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - The exit-criteria checkboxes are mostly unchecked; only the \\\"no prose-keyword heuristics\\\" item is checked.\\n  - Parked: PR-4 dedup owner (#832).\\n  - Owner-gated:\\n    - Git history rewrite.\\n    - LFS quota.\\n    - Size-ratchet flip-to-enforcing (dated 2026-09-01).\\n    - ui-split stage 2+ (tui #282).\\n    - The gact-tui submodule pin bump.\\n    - P14 `tmp/` cleanups.\\n    - The wire-type codegen decision (tui #254).\\n    - A follow-up truthfulness pass on `CLIO_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`.\\n- **Related:** `codex-rework-landing-2026-08.md` cites this doc (\\\"house rule; cf. `system-cleanup-2026-07.md`\\\") and inherits its ratchet rules.\\n\\n### 7. `codex-rework-landing-2026-08.md`\\n- **Status:** ACTIVE, approved 2026-08-25. The latest dated record is 2026-09-01. This is the Codex (agent executor) A2UI/v0.3 rework landing campaign, not the Codex sandbox.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Land four repos on develop (main for marketplace and clio-kit) through green-CI PRs.\\n  - **Ground rules:**\\n    - No silent fallback.\\n    - No ratchet raises.\\n    - Tests first.\\n    - The server owns semantics.\\n    - Two-lane observability.\\n    - Protocol by negotiation.\\n  - **Phases 0–6:**\\n    - Phase 0: draft PRs and the issue set.\\n    - Phase 1: Flowcept/CMF absorption.\\n    - Phase 2: W1–W4 backend work.\\n    - Phase 3: W8–W15 frontend work.\\n    - Phase 4: W7 clio-schemas contract.\\n    - Phase 5: marketplace and clio-kit.\\n    - Phase 6: strict merge order.\\n  - Seven owner decisions, all resolved. The campaign stops at develop with no release.\\n- **Builds on:**\\n  - `system-cleanup-2026-07.md`.\\n  - `feat/flowcept-provenance`, which is already on develop via PR #1248; the branch was deleted.\\n  - Umbrellas clio-agent #1249, gact-tui #371, marketplace #54 and clio-kit #381.\\n  - PRs clio-agent #1255, gact-tui #380, marketplace #56 and clio-kit #383.\\n  - Old contract `CANONICAL-CONVERSATION.md`, which the new W12 render contract replaces.\\n  - clio-schemas PR #5 (0.2.2) and the earlier #1247 and #1188/#353.\\n- **Left open (named, non-blocking, in the 2026-09-01 record):**\\n  - A one-off session-status flicker.\\n  - `surface.error` and state-enum slots without producers.\\n  - 13 inert diagnostic pipelines on cmf-server.\\n  - The spotter watcher's typed `campaign_store_unavailable`.\\n  - Win32-pinned snapshot PNGs.\\n  - The model sometimes minting new A2UI surface ids.\\n  - The merge gate still lists pending explicit reviewer approvals and the develop merges. This file does not record those as done.\\n  - Qualification limitations (local ARC fallback, absent relay config, two `stream_completed_without_chunks` turns) were typed warnings, not green evidence.\\n  - A service-stop confirmation for port 8281 was not obtained.\\n- **Supersession notes:**\\n  - A record correction pins the marketplace gitlink to `2a44f200`, replacing the earlier `2c1f1866`.\\n  - The 192→203 route forecast is stale; the actual count was 205.\\n  - Review-blocker lists changed over time: the 2026-08-28 four blockers were mostly fixed, and the 2026-09-01 re-review found 92 findings \\\"all fixed, zero deferred\\\".\\n\\n## Topic group D: installation and local models\\n\\n### 8. `installation-and-storage-recovery.md`\\n- **Status:** no date or status line stated. It references issues #1782 and #1783 and Core 2.3.2.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - **Older Linux hosts (#1782):** use a private, checksum-pinned Ubuntu 22.04 C/C++ runtime and an explicit ELF-loader launcher. Downloads retry at most three times within ",
