  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading guide: eight design docs in `design/`\\n\\n**Coverage caveat.** The shell was refused as read-only, so I could not chunk the files with `tail`/`head`. I read `roadmap.md`, `beta2-integration-qualification-2026-10-03.md` and `blueprint-core-coordination.md` completely. For the other five I read the first ~12K characters of each, then the rest through line-numbered search windows. The unread parts are listed under \\\"Not read\\\" at the end. Dates come from the files themselves, and where a file gives none I say so.\\n\\n## Chronological chain\\n\\n1. `roadmap.md`: v1 ARC plane done; the later threads are scoped. It carries a 2026-09-17 banner.\\n2. `unified-arc-highway.md`: design dated 2026-07-11/12, with status lines edited as late as the 2026-09 agent-loop rebuild.\\n3. `v010-program-2026-08.md`: status line \\\"ACTIVE, 2026-07-30\\\". The filename says 2026-08.\\n4. `v010-slices-2026-08.md`: issue-tree expansion of the program doc. It cites the program doc on develop at `1c8e39fd` and owner statements dated 2026-07-30.\\n5. `campaign-integration-landing-2026-09.md`: the September references and child-interaction wave. Marketplace PR #59 merged 2026-09-03.\\n6. `beta2-integration-qualification-2026-10-03.md`: 2026-10-03.\\n7. `beta3-integration-status.md`: checkpoints dated October 4 and October 5. It supersedes its own \\\"do not publish\\\" hold.\\n8. `blueprint-core-coordination.md`: **undated**. It cites Core PRs #1273/#1274 and the registry/blueprint work, which fits the beta-3 era. That placement is inference, not stated.\\n\\nThe v0.10 program and slices docs and the highway doc all date from July, so the order among them is partly overlap. The highway design is the earliest and is independent of the v0.10 UI/MCP program.\\n\\n## Best entry point\\n\\n**`v010-program-2026-08.md`** is the best single entry point.\\n- It states the thesis, the program structure and the owner decisions D1–D3, then lays out phases P0–P5 and a deletion inventory.\\n- It names the repos and the issues the other docs refer back to.\\n- The slices doc is its expansion.\\n- `roadmap.md` is shorter, but it covers only the ARC plane and is the least current.\\n- The highway doc is the right second read for anyone touching messages, sessions or ARC internals.\\n\\n## Per-file findings\\n\\n### 1. `roadmap.md`\\n**Group:** ARC live context plane. **Status:** no date of its own. A banner says the A2UI 0.9.1 compatibility campaign (S0–S9) completed 2026-09-17 (umbrella #1363). It also says v1 is done and green on real ALCF.\\n\\n- **Decided:** v1, the single-node logical plane, is finished. The remaining arc is written as a dependency graph of threads rather than a timeline. Thread B, a clio-core backend behind a `make_arc_store(config)` factory, is the suggested lead. Thread A, exposing ARC state over REST for the TUI, is the parallel companion.\\n- **Builds on:** `GOAL.md`, `docs/archive/arc-live-context-plane.md`, `docs/archive/implementation-spec.md` and `docs/design/compaction-checkpoint-1339.md` (#1339). The #1339 note says the v1 compaction path destroyed the human-visible transcript and amplified the `_events/m` atom lane Θ(N²) per append.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - Thread D (the CEE MCP) needs B.\\n  - Thread C (richer testing) is ongoing.\\n  - Thread E (the distributed team and the physical KV plane) is the far horizon and needs B and D.\\n  - No owners or dates are given for any thread.\\n\\n### 2. `unified-arc-highway.md`\\n**Group:** ARC / message and session unification. **Status:** first consumer live (2026-07-12; loop later replaced by `ClioReAct`). The next consumer is explicitly \\\"not started — do not claim\\\". It is an internals refactor with no `src/` change.\\n\\n- **Decided:** one operation-sourced log, with the four current stores (persistence, context, SSE and search/tree indexes) becoming thin projections of it.\\n  - The external contract is frozen: SSE vocabulary, `/messages` reload equals live, context semantics, search, trace replay, `arc.op`, compaction wire, delegation envelope, memory stats.\\n  - Migration is a 7-step strangler, one consumer at a time, with session-scoped rollback and no big-bang cutover.\\n  - The review corrected the draft in two ways. C1: a raw append lane and new message/part atom kinds are required. C2: write-path changes need a live dual-run A/B harness, because the captured corpus cannot validate them.\\n  - Ingest becomes must-succeed-or-typed-fail in the same step that removes an old write path.\\n  - Owner ruling 2026-07-12: clio-core is the default home of the log, with loud degradation to LocalFS.\\n- **Builds on:** #737 (thesis), #893 (umbrella, memory profile `893_memory_profile.md`), #889 (boot index-only fix), #901, #880, #767 PR3 (commit `9078aa2`, already delivered step 3), #762, #736–#733, and #891/#895/#890/#892 as non-goals or prerequisites. It also cites the SPEC sections and code paths in its claim ledger.\\n- **Open (§5.2 questions, each with a recommendation):**\\n  - Q2: streaming live-edge atom, recommended last.\\n  - Q3: moving secret redaction to the write path. It needs a precision check on the credential detector.\\n  - Q4: persistence-by-reference versus `reload == live`. It is a gate; if 4.1.A cannot go green, step 5 does not ship.\\n  - Q6: compaction archive semantics move to durable replay. **Owner sign-off is required**, and it is the one owned exception to \\\"change nothing observable\\\".\\n  - Q8: first-GET rehydration cost. A checkpoint atom is provisioned but implemented only if the budget is missed.\\n  - Q9: the sunset TTL for legacy sessions. The owner must confirm it.\\n  - Q1 is marked resolved.\\n\\n### 3. `v010-program-2026-08.md`\\n**Group:** v0.10 program (MCP v2, federation, Session v3 UI). **Status:** ACTIVE, 2026-07-30. All owner decisions D1–D3 are closed.\\n\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - **Structure:** one umbrella with five phase subtrees and hard phase gates. P0–P2 ship as 0.10.0-alpha tags; v0.10.0 cuts after P5. Nothing merges to main until the composed gate is green.\\n  - **D1:** gact-tui becomes a multi-connection client. Primary agents are reached over user-provided tunnels, and there is no hub. Remote subagents go through the backend's own relay semantics. A bearer auth scheme is added server-side.\\n  - **D2:** Option A, a shared schema package, `clio-schemas`. gact-tui generates its TS types from the exported JSON Schema.\\n  - **D3:** Codex is the default implementer for token economy. Claude owns orchestration, merges and review. All reviews are cross-vendor.\\n  - **Other decisions:**\\n    - The sampling pillar is dead.\\n    - One spawn primitive replaces the split tools.\\n    - Documents and Live Web are in scope.\\n    - The UI is built kit-first.\\n    - The mcp_ui_sciences corpus is the upstream spec for P3.\\n    - P3.4 requires UI-level artifact interaction through one annotation primitive.\\n- **Builds on:** the Session v3 prototype, MCP 2026-07-28 with SEP-2663 and SEP-1865, `openai/codex-plugin-cc`, #948 and #671 (absorbed by P2), the #1031 gate harness (PR #1095), #966 lineage data, #974 egress, gact-tui#318 and the cc_dispatch / mcp_ui_sciences sessions. It also cites the relay v1.5.9 evidence bundles and `snapshot/mcp-decomposition-2026-07`.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - The Codex worker-fleet lane is marked \\\"research pending\\\".\\n  - Codex-as-MCP-tasks-client is unconfirmed, and nothing depends on it.\\n  - Office rendering is a model-rendered floor; the LibreOffice builder is a deferred, designed-for tier.\\n  - The Live Web design workspace is deferred past 0.10.\\n  - Email integration is a seams-only future pillar.\\n  - Relay-side asks (identity, elicitation producer, `remote_agent`) are filed but non-blocking.\\n  - The gact-tui contract change (GACT v0.3) is listed in §3b but is not specified here.\\n\\n### 4. `v010-slices-2026-08.md`\\n**Group:** v0.10 program (slice plan). **Status:** a planning pass whose approval mints the issue tree. It says all D1–D3 are closed.\\n\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - The slice trees per phase are P0 (8–9 slices), P1 (9), P2 (16), P3 (7), P4 (10) and P5 (3). Each slice carries scope, acceptance, deletions, dependencies, size and lane. The mint plan is about 55 slice issues.\\n  - **Changed since the program doc:** P4 is now a fresh React 18 + Vite rebuild of the view layer. The program doc said Solid. `@clio/core` and Tauri are kept, and the legacy view tree is deleted wholesale at cutover.\\n  - **Key finding:** installed mcp 1.26.0 speaks 2025-11-25, so the P0.3 upgrade gates all of P1.\\n  - **Defaults adopted:** annotation is one part; child elicitation is parent-forward; placement is a per-spawn parameter; runs reuse `AgentTaskRegistry`; `clio-schemas` uses lockstep exact-version pins.\\n- **Builds on:** the program doc on develop at `1c8e39fd`, #671 (`ExpertInvoker` already exists in `gact/agents/invoker.py`), #1031/PR #1095, #966, #974, the mcp_ui_sciences CONTRACT.md and the cc_dispatch scenarios.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - Risk: P0.3 is a hard stop if fastmcp 4 does not negotiate 2026-07-28. The fallback is vendoring the SDK's experimental modules.\\n  - Risk: the elicitation pause must use an async-safe permission-gate variant.\\n  - Owner questions carried to mint: url-mode trust source (P3 origin-grants or P1-local); the `clio-schemas` home (later \\\"adopted\\\" as a new iowarp repo); and whether the cluster ships a gact runtime for the remote child.\\n  - Also carried: which relay lane produces the gate's post-admission round, and whether the fastmcp-tasks client wrapper lives in P1 or P2.\\n  - The P2.8 wrap-or-build risk is flagged.\\n\\n### 5. `campaign-integration-landing-2026-09.md`\\n**Group:** campaign landing record. **Status:** LANDING. The fix train AF1 → AF-FOLD → AF-IMG → AF-FINAL is complete on `review/campaign-backend`, PR #1298 → develop. Marketplace PR #59 is merged at `22a0cea8` (2026-09-03). gact-tui PR #387 is open and gated separately.\\n\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - The reviewed heads were NOT MERGEABLE AS-IS, so the clio-agent and gact-tui lanes were fixed forward, not rebuilt.\\n  - The review found five blocker classes:\\n    1. event-loop work;\\n    2. unbounded in-process state;\\n    3. fabricated attribution or capability;\\n    4. degradations that only reached logs;\\n    5. scope and vocabulary holes.\\n  - Rulings from folding Codex's undisclosed push `ad7ecf7b`: refuse-and-retain over drain, and an invalid-status store boundary. Evidence-not-fabrication is the guiding principle for the provider paths.\\n  - Seven escaped tunables were migrated to config; 17 new keys are config-resolved.\\n- **Builds on:** `composer-pipeline-landing-2026-09.md` (not amended), `system-cleanup-2026-07.md` as the house-rule reference, PR #1298/#387/#59, the P3.1 slice, and issues gact-tui #324 and marketplace #61/#62.\\n- **Open (§e):**\\n  - Two load-flaky streaming tests are attributed to the streaming-lifecycle lane and to be adjudicated on CI.\\n  - The restart reshape is lossy for legacy question rows: empty `turn_id`/`attempt_id`, and `resume_on_answer` forced true. It is recorded, not patched.\\n  - Marketplace #61 (the parent factorio pack has the same defect classes) and #62 (`check_model_pins.py` misses a bare `model:` pin).\\n  - gact-tui #324 is folded into P3.1.\\n  - The full suite was not run locally; it is deferred to CI.\\n\\n### 6. `beta2-integration-qualification-2026-10-03.md`\\n**Group:** release qualification. **Status:** 2026-10-03. Agent 0.9.5b2, UI 0.11.3-beta.4, clio-schemas 0.5.3. It says CI conclusions on the release PRs remain authoritative.\\n\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - It records the integrated beta-2 qualification: live Codex Luna and Astra runs that built linked scatter/map/table views from a 500-row CSV, plus browser review.\\n  - It also records focused backend, UI and website passes, and the macOS native packaging gate (workflow `37166419334`).\\n  - A beta-update channel is added, and Desktop beta 1 needs one manual upgrade.\\n  - Earlier failed trials are kept in local evidence, not counted as passes.\\n- **Builds on:** `a",
