  "preview": "{\"answer\": \"# Reading guide notes: seven SDK design files\\n\\n**Coverage caveat.** I did not read all seven files in full. Each read was cut at 12,000 characters, and I filled in with heading maps and targeted context searches. I read the openings, the heading structure, the defaults and Done sections, and parts of the ledgers. The middle sections of the plans and most ledger rows beyond those shown are unread. Open-items lines below only cover what I saw. \\\"None stated\\\" means none stated in the parts I read, not none in the file.\\n\\n## 1. acceptance-ledger.md\\n- **Date/status:** Qualification defects dated 2026-10-23/24 and a security review dated 2026-10-22. Group: Plugins, SDK and flows (the megachange).\\n- **What it records:** The evidence ledger for the plugins, Agent SDK and flows megachange. Rows follow `megachange-plan.md`, and a row passes only with recorded evidence. Statuses are `passed (live)`, `tests only`, `static`, `done`, `open` and `blocked`.\\n- **Contents:** Decisions D1–D40, phase rows (P0-1 onward), live scenarios, a K-numbered defect list, a security review (S-1 to S-11) and platform rows.\\n- **Decisions seen:**\\n  - D1: no new `TaskKind`.\\n  - D2: handoff not implemented.\\n  - D5: `run_code`, `rlm` and `code` flows out of scope.\\n  - D9: remote agents not built.\\n  - D21: plugin-change delivery, with `plugin-change-delivery.md` as the next step.\\n  - D30: `run_plan` renamed to `run_workflow`.\\n  - D36: a full reinstall is required, with no upgrade path.\\n  - D40: `response_parts` retained separately from the final answer, citing issue #1857.\\n- **Builds on:** `megachange-plan.md`, `plugin-change-delivery.md`, and clio-agent issue #1857.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - X-1 (Tauri desktop), X-2 (Windows-only paths) and X-3 (HPC over SSH) are `blocked` because a cloud session cannot run them.\\n  - K-10 is open: the `core.tasks` and `core.guidelines` fragments exceed the 150-token budget.\\n  - S-10 is open and needs the person's decision: loopback privileged routes can be reached by any local process, including a command the agent runs.\\n  - S-11 is accepted as low risk.\\n  - K-24 is fixed by tests but was not re-read live.\\n  - The grep for `| open |` returned no matches, so the only explicit open rows I found are those listed here.\\n- **Relationships:** It is the base ledger. The plan docs below cite its decisions D1–D29 as still in force.\\n\\n## 2. delegation-fork-science-plan.md\\n- **Date/status:** Base `develop` at `8159955f5`. The Done list is the goal condition. Addendum A was folded in on 2026-10-27, so this plan now governs. Group: Delegation, fork and science log.\\n- **What it decided:** Seven workstreams:\\n  1. Default delegation: an omitted `agent` spawns `self`, plus generic `explore`, `planner` and `review` roles.\\n  2. Fork: agent self-fork.\\n  3. Science log: typed entries with Observations citing recorded calls.\\n  4. Wordle study.\\n  5. Hidden-law study.\\n  6. Export of flows and subagents.\\n  7. Publication on clio.iowarp.ai.\\n- **Rules it states:** Delete and replace, with no shims. The task layer is the only execution authority. The platform provides facts, not judgements. Hidden answers are never written to the workspace. Generic plugins contain nothing domain-specific.\\n- **Out of scope:** Remote agents, `run_code` and `rlm`, statistics inside the log, solvers for the studies, git worktrees, and an HDF5 tuning study.\\n- **Builds on:** #1825 (plugins/SDK/flows on `develop`), `acceptance-ledger.md`, `model-fleet-ledger.md`, `memory-ledger.md`, `plugins-and-composition.md`, `agent-sdk.md`, `orchestration-semantics.md`, `model-fleet.md`, and `site/WRITING.md`.\\n- **Left open:** A \\\"Defaults for the open questions\\\" table, to be recorded in the science ledger. Examples: showcase model, reframe approval, and invalid-guess handling. The Done list requires scenarios F1–F25 to pass. If the session cannot create the release, large exports are blocked on release rights. Merging to `main` is not part of the plan, but the cut-off text was truncated, so I did not confirm that.\\n- **Relationships:** Addendum A is folded into it. `science-ledger.md` is its evidence ledger.\\n\\n## 3. delegation-fork-science-addendum-a.md\\n- **Date/status:** \\\"Folded into delegation-fork-science-plan.md on 2026-10-27; this file records the decisions.\\\" Group: Delegation, fork and science log.\\n- **What it decided:**\\n  - Observations cite tool calls via `from_calls`, and the log fills in lineage and artifacts.\\n  - Measured values are handed to the agent as data, through `query_log` and a new `export_measurements` (Parquet or CSV).\\n  - Claims cite the analysis call that produced them.\\n  - Every branch reads the whole study but writes only its own branch.\\n  - Isolated workspaces are available with `isolate: true`, and fork folders are cloned copy-on-write.\\n  - The log has no built-in \\\"better\\\".\\n- **Builds on:** the plan above, the artifact registry's `TransformRecord`, and `runtime/sandbox_roots.py`.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - Plugin MCP servers (the `fleet` profile) that write files on their own are not confined per node. It is recorded as a decision (FD19), and plugin authors are told to take output paths as arguments.\\n  - Branches that read each other's claims can converge early. The method skill mitigates this.\\n  - Programmatic tool calling is a separate item, and nothing is reserved for it.\\n  - F11, F13 and F15 must be re-run after this landed, and earlier runs are superseded and not published.\\n- **Relationships:** It supersedes the plan's earlier visibility rule (\\\"none while running\\\", ancestors only). It is now authoritative only as the decision record.\\n\\n## 4. long-term-memory-plan.md\\n- **Date/status:** Base `claude/sdk-plugins-flows`, \\\"or its merge target\\\". No date seen. Group: Long-term memory.\\n- **What it decided:**\\n  - Six workstreams: store and search on clio-core, tools and read path, background pass, export and import, memory page and in-chat surfaces, usage tracking.\\n  - Memory is Markdown subject documents in categories: profile, preferences, topics, areas, people, environments. Each fact is a line with an id and a source.\\n  - It lives on clio-core through `ARCStore` in the `memory` namespace, with BM25 retrieval.\\n  - Background changes are proposals, and the `memory_` prefix means long-term memory only.\\n  - Defaults: 2,000-token index cap, 30-minute idle trigger with at least 3 user messages, 60-day expiry, sensitive topics off.\\n- **Builds on:** `acceptance-ledger.md` D1–D29, `plugins-and-composition.md`, `agent-sdk.md`, `orchestration-semantics.md`, `docs/ARC_MEMORY_LAYER.md`, clio-core #905 (the indexer), and #771.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - It says the delegation, fork and science plan named in an earlier draft was never written, so its F decisions do not apply. This conflicts with the existence of `delegation-fork-science-plan.md`, which uses `F` ids.\\n  - The blocker was that the default clio-core config did not compose the indexer, so search silently returned zero hits.\\n  - Out of scope: embeddings, shared or federated memory, and generating skills from lessons.\\n- **Relationships:** `memory-ledger.md` is its evidence ledger, with `MD` ids.\\n\\n## 5. memory-ledger.md\\n- **Date/status:** Live scenarios run 2026-10-23. Group: Long-term memory.\\n- **What it records:** Decisions MD0–MD43 (at least), phase rows, a rename inventory, live scenarios M1–M18, a re-run after the base merge, and final qualification on the merged code.\\n- **Final state:** Every decision and scenario I saw is `passed`. M1–M18 pass, covering indexer search, the snapshot, concurrent updates (409 `memory_conflict`), restart resume, and the memory page at both viewport sizes.\\n- **Decisions seen:**\\n  - MD1: the indexer is bound through `CLIO_CTE_POOL`.\\n  - MD9: companion-blob shrink fix.\\n  - MD14: one protected human doc keeps the old tool names.\\n  - MD15: the marketplace `memory` plugin was deleted.\\n  - MD17: draft PRs are clio-agent#1835, gact-tui#674 and marketplace#110.\\n  - MD23: the opt-in explicit memory search injection was removed.\\n- **Builds on:** `long-term-memory-plan.md`.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - M8 had no `explore` agent installed, so the check used a general subagent instead.\\n  - Platform rows are present, and there is a \\\"Found outside this change\\\" section. I did not read either.\\n- **Relationships:** The plan governs. This ledger overrides it where a decision row says the plan was wrong, per the plan's own rule.\\n\\n## 6. science-ledger.md\\n- **Date/status:** Phase 0 exports from the `.cloud-run/phase0/` runs. Several rows still show `pending`. Group: Delegation, fork and science log.\\n- **What it records:** Decisions FD1–FD34, a subagent verdict table (FD13), a Phase 0 export baseline, and scenarios F1 onward. Prompts are labelled as mechanism (tool-directed) or plain request.\\n- **Final state, as far as I read:**\\n  - Passed: FD1, FD2, FD4, FD10–FD19, FD21–FD24 and FD29–FD34, and mechanism scenarios F1–F5.\\n  - Pending: FD3 (reframe approval), FD5–FD9, and FD20 (branch/PR setup).\\n  - FD8 changes the showcase model to an Opus-class Claude, away from the plan's Sonnet-class default. Evidence is in `.cloud-run/f13/attempts.md`.\\n  - FD13 verdicts: keep `critic`, `evidence_critic` and `independent_reviewer`; delete `data_analysis_expert`.\\n- **Known limits stated:**\\n  - FD19: shared plugin servers are not confined per node.\\n  - FD33: a same-user process can read another process's `/proc/<pid>/environ`.\\n  - FD34: the live \\\"shadow\\\" of the agent's law is not drawn. The held-out replay is produced for the export and the site instead.\\n  - Phase 0 export gaps: flow runs read \\\"Not started yet\\\" offline, and subagent trees are appended flat.\\n- **Builds on:** the plan, Addendum A, and the export design.\\n- **Left open:** F-scenario rows beyond F5 were not read.\\n- **Relationships:** It is the evidence ledger for the plan and the addendum.\\n\\n## 7. windows-openai-qualification.md\\n- **Date/status:** Run 2026-10-24/25. **Overall: fail.** The 48-hour semantic qualification runs 2026-10-25 04:50 UTC to 2026-10-27 04:50 UTC. Group: Qualification and platform (Windows, Codex sign-in).\\n- **What it records:** A Windows qualification with Codex sign-in. The first journey asked Deep Researcher for a storage decision and failed before producing a report.\\n- **Defects found:**\\n  - #1855: concurrent plugin-cache staging race, repaired.\\n  - #1857: the critic received only addenda. Source repaired, but the live repeat is pending.\\n  - #1856: workspace consent released only one of 17 parked requests. Source repaired, live repeat pending.\\n  - #1849: queued-call token budget.\\n  - Others: #1850, #1851, #1852, #1853 and #1847 (fixed here), and gact-tui#677–#681.\\n- **Builds on:** `acceptance-ledger.md` D40, and the issues and PRs above.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - The repaired source must be live-repeated for #1857, #1856, #1849 and the permission-card refinements.\\n  - #1850, #1852, #1853, #1851, and gact-tui#677–#679 are open.\\n  - The report is explicit that its mechanism receipts do not establish research quality.\\n  - Only focused validation was done. It claims neither full CI nor desktop release validation.\\n- **Relationships:** It is a standalone qualification record. It feeds `acceptance-ledger.md` D40.\\n\\n## Cross-file notes\\n- **Ledger and plan pairs:**\\n  - `acceptance-ledger.md` goes with `megachange-plan.md`.\\n  - `memory-ledger.md` goes with `long-term-memory-plan.md`.\\n  - `science-ledger.md` goes with the delegation plan and Addendum A.\\n- **Discrepancy:** The memory plan says the delegation plan \\\"was never written\\\", yet `delegation-fork-science-plan.md` exists and cites `memory-ledger.md`. The memory ledger MD0 records the same \\\"never written\\\" check as of 2026-10-23. A new contributor should read the memory docs as written before the delegation plan landed.\\n\\nSuggested topic groups are as given in each entry.\", \"error_info\": null, \"expert_handoffs\": [",
