d CI stay unqualified.\\n\\n## 13. `task-replacement-r38-corrections.md`, group: Startup/initialization\\n- **Status:** the combined R37 review is NO-GO (Astra found two defects, Fable supported the architecture). Initial construction only.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - A child's own startup warning is delivered through trusted same-session input, not subscriber authorization.\\n  - Uncertain startup cleanup is retained as a nonterminal observation, and the admission, promotion and assignment-creation paths check it.\\n  - Delete `delegation_return.py` and add it to the static denylist.\\n  - `message_intents.py` is classified as historical decoding only.\\n- **Builds on:** R37, R2's removal manifest, and N10/N11.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - F03 history-scan, staging and whole-session-write costs.\\n  - Fable's lingering-attention concern.\\n  - Legacy tests that still import the deleted mutable store must be rewritten.\\n  - Another review must cover previously unread source paths.\\n\\n## 14. `task-replacement-r39-corrections.md`, group: Native/external/test migration\\n- **Status:** \\\"implementation/regression construction, not runtime acceptance.\\\" Parent core `27b3a381`, GACT `41660185`.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Native cancellation keeps its SDK identity until canonical `terminal_at`.\\n  - A fresh cancelled reply restores nonterminal cleanup progress after validating custody.\\n  - Rebuild the nullable-spawn tests over the real FastMCP boundary.\\n  - Restore document autosave coalescing through the Core mailbox.\\n  - Correct the Factorio prompt.\\n  - Preserve the provider and presentation tests, removing only the retired relay case.\\n- **Builds on:** R38 (review process 24400), and Astra's SDK adjudication.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - The legacy stdio/SSE inline-input attribution defect remains open.\\n  - 37 of 1,093 test files still import missing or retired items (AST inventory, not pytest collection).\\n  - The R38 review's 348,521-byte disposable runtime is manu