maining sections now.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_7970e4dc3ccc\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"I still need the plan's tail sections and the end of r32, which the displayed output cut off.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_f21fed20c640\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"answer\"}, \"text\": \"# Reading guide: task-replacement series (17 files)\\n\\n**Where I looked:** all 17 files under `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/`.\\n\\n**Coverage gaps:**\\n- The plan (64,964 bytes) and r32 (12,058 bytes) exceeded the display cap. I read their top sections in full. For the later sections I used line-numbered search with context, so a few long lines (plan lines 62, 75, 79, 83, 85, 89, 95, 112, 116, 130, 136, 138, 140, 144, 396 and the tail of 405) were cut off mid-sentence.\\n- I did not read the plan's module-by-module removal tables (about lines 193–333). I saw only their headings and a few rows.\\n- Nothing in the series gives a date except the plan's 2026-10-13 preflight and Oct 14 target, and r32's \\\"October 15 source progress\\\". \\\"Status\\\" below is what each file says about itself.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. `task-replacement-plan.md` (revision R2), group: Foundation contract\\n- **Status:** target release Oct 14 (America/Chicago). Preflight receipt dated 2026-10-13. The target is explicitly not permission to bypass acceptance.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Delete the old task integration first, then rebuild around one typed `TaskSnapshot`, one confirmed Core writer and one recipient-input record as the only delivery acknowledgement.\\n  - Native execution goes through FastMCP/Docket. The pinned tuple is FastMCP/fastmcp-tasks 4.1.0, MCP 2.0.0, Docket 0.26.2.\\n  - The conversation engine alone decides assignment transitions. Relay becomes an ordinary MCP server.\\n  - No old-engine fallback, stubs or archives. A deliberately broken removal commit stays local with draft PRs.\\n  - Acceptance is gated on Q1–Q9 live families, six races (R1–R6) repeated five times each, CI, and migration idempotence.\\n- **Builds on:** baseline core `5475042f` / GACT `32044a38`, and the protected human design docs (`subagent-lifecycle-and-session-messaging.md`, `agent-task-architecture-review-2026-10-12.md`, `session-recall-and-long-term-memory.md`). Later sections cite removal reviews and \\\"R30\\\" Astra review.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - If gates fail, no release.\\n  - Provider-continuation reattachment was pending implementation and Claude source review (line 405).\\n  - Local-transfer interruption is an explicit migration/native-recovery requirement (W01/N12).\\n  - Relay migration is explicitly not promised.\\n  - Startup-replay and performance optimizations are deferred to measurement (Q8).\\n  - Live-model availability was only a credentials check, not acceptance.\\n\\n## 2. `task-replacement-corrections-r19.md`, group: Retained-behavior corrections\\n- **Status:** packet addressing Astra R17 and Claude R18. Behavioral tests held until initial implementation.\\n- **Decided:** eight corrections C1–C8 within existing owners:\\n  - Restore an absent same-session context from validated evidence only.\\n  - Route every plan-Question close through one resolver.\\n  - Resolve stale Question answers against historical identities.\\n  - Bind pause holds to their assignment.\\n  - Resume workflows from saved checkpoints.\\n  - Add an owner-local workflow deadline timer.\\n  - Allow linked workflow retry.\\n  - Keep strict settlement for unknown external cancellation.\\n- **Builds on:** R2, the Astra and Claude R17/R18 reviews, and the reports `task-replacement-correction-plan-astra-r19.md` / `-claude-r19.md`.\\n- **Left open:**\\n  - An optional human decision on amending R2 to allow an authenticated restart past unresolved cancellation. This is pending and not implemented.\\n  - Short-control Core cost (Q8).\\n  - Claude's suggestion to count external acknowledgement as settlement was rejected, not adopted.\\n\\n## 3. `task-replacement-corrections-r21.md`, group: Retained-behavior corrections\\n- **Status:** completes the R20 source-review set. Frozen base core `f020a591`, GACT `ce993164`, marketplace `9257bba5`. Both reviewers r",
