able with `_meta: {\\\"x-clio-agent/audience\\\": \\\"agent\\\"}`, and the default is the human.\\n  - CLIO advertises the `x-clio-agent/agent-driven-elicitation` extension. The server gates its size-guard on it.\\n  - Global enable defaults ON, with a per-server deny list.\\n  - Agent fulfilment is a tool-less bounded child turn whose answer is schema-validated. Every failure falls back to the human.\\n  - The \\\"semantic firewall\\\" forbids this from becoming sampling.\\n  - `url`-mode elicitation is out of scope.\\n- **Builds on:** Issues #1114 (MRTR / SEP-2322), #1309 (agent-driven elicitation, C1-S7) and #1325 (size-guard use case). SEP-2577 and fastmcp ≥ 4.0 (`4.0.0b5` baseline).\\n- **Open or deferred:**\\n  - It states no explicit open items.\\n  - It flags a risk that reading the SDK alone misleads (it misled two passes on #1325).\\n  - It records recursion depth as bounded (default 1).\\n  - It notes the extension closed a past negotiation gap.\\n- **Supersession:** None stated. It is related to doc 1's note that external MCP `input_required` reaches the question surface, and to doc 7 for the human side.\\n\\n### 9. `agent-communication-campaign-notes.md`\\n- **Status and date:** \\\"Written 2026-09-11 … Not a plan.\\\" The code references are to the release-stack tip `fix/1339-compaction-checkpoint` and should be re-verified against `develop`.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Mostly records facts and judgments. One recorded owner decision (2026-09-11) is that the `observe_agent_tasks` title goes back to \\\"Observe\\\". \\\"Get status\\\" is reserved for a different tool.\\n  - It recommends a split between discovery (`get_status`) and observation, but frames these as items to decide.\\n- **Builds on:**\\n  - #1339 (level 9) and #1000 (OBSERVE posture), commit 88cf6bb0.\\n  - #948 and `docs/design/agents-creating-agents-2026-07.md`.\\n  - Codex commits e76c6726, 7fac63a7, 848e32e2 and 745a8d81 (the retitle).\\n  - clio-relay `relay_observe`.\\n- **Open or deferred (§4):**\\n  - Split `get_status` from `observe_agent_tasks`.\\n  - Async monitor shape: monitor ids, several outstanding, wake via CONTINUE.\\n  - Add a cancel tool.\\n  - Fix the row vocabulary and title table.\\n  - A2A / ACP mapping that keeps wait, observe and continue explicit.\\n  - Stale mentions of `check_agent_tasks` in `CLAUDE.md` and in the `get_agent_task_output` argument description.\\n  - §5 lists tests to add.\\n- **Supersession:** Partly overtaken by doc 2/doc 1. Those docs introduce `cancel_tasks`, shared `wait_tasks`/`observe_tasks` and an automatic wake, and say legacy `wait_agent_tasks`/`observe_agent_tasks` aliases only delegate and are removed the following release. That answers its \\\"no cancel tool\\\" gap. The notes are dated before those task docs (2026-10-10 and later), so read them as historical context.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Suggested reading order and cross-doc notes\\n1. Doc 2 (the task contract) → doc 1 (v3 rebuild) → doc 3 (transcript access) → doc 4 (lifecycle and messaging).\\n2. Then doc 5 (steering), doc 7 → 8 (questions and elicitation), and doc 6 (turn transcript) as a separate track.\\n3. Doc 9 last, as history.\\n\\n## Not verified\\n- `../qualification/agent-facing-tasks-use-cases.md` was not opened.\\n- The unread regions listed above may contain further open items.\", \"error_info\": null, \"expert_handoffs\": [], \"response_parts\": [{\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_04993749e62f\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"\\n\\n\\nI'll start by checking file sizes.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_396e661f2aa9\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"Shell is blocked (read-only), so I'll use the file reader directly.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_fdbe9826cb85\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"The first read truncated four files (1, 2, 4 and