 and the \\\"problem\\\" and \\\"invariant\\\" sections. I did not read §3.3, §4, §5 and §6 (PR-by-PR migration, about lines 189–360).\\n- **`subagent-lifecycle-and-session-messaging.md`:** I read lines 1–~232 (one gap) and 232–386. I did not read \\\"Pause, Stop, cancel and restart\\\" and \\\"Proposed model-facing controls\\\" (about lines 250–310) except their first lines.\\n\\nStatements below come from what I read. Where a file's open items might sit in an unread region, I say so.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Topic group A: Agent-facing async tasks (core contract and replacement)\\n\\n### 1. `agent-task-native-v3.md`\\n- **Status and date:** No date or status line.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Rebuild the task integration around native execution (FastMCP Tasks for Shell/Download/Indexing) and CLIO's conversation engine for agent assignments.\\n  - Keep the shared tools `query_tasks`, `observe_tasks`, `wait_tasks`, `cancel_tasks` and `get_task_result`.\\n  - Add a Question kind: `ask_user` returns a durable handle at once, and `wait_tasks(question_handle)` waits unbounded by default.\\n  - Persist submissions before invoking the backend. Recovery promises honest uncertainty, not exactly-once effects.\\n  - Use one admission path and one Core-backed mailbox per session. Sessions are stable addresses, and `assignment_disposition=\\\"yield\\\"|\\\"complete\\\"` separates a turn ending from an assignment ending.\\n  - Remove, rather than wrap, the old schedulers, wake policies and custody modules (§4).\\n- **Builds on:** The branch `codex/agent-facing-async-tasks` (the work in doc 2), \\\"GACT\\\" and Docket/FastMCP. It builds on the existing question owner, TurnRunner and Core hierarchy and writer. It cites no numbered issues in what I read.\\n- **Open or deferred:**\\n  - The Question extension is \\\"an implementation and qualification gate\\\" to be verified with actual models before it counts as complete.\\n  - Distributed agent hosting \\\"does not qualify\\\" locally. It needs