  "preview": "d live-qualified against Flowcept plus CMF\\\", August 2026.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Spotter is a standalone, read-only MCP for agent provenance queries. It is our own interface, not a proxy of the Flowcept or CMF MCPs.\\n  - Provider selection is deployment config, never a tool argument.\\n  - There is no silent fallback; the typed error is `capability_unavailable`.\\n  - The UI keeps a separate REST path through clio-agent, and gact-tui never calls Spotter.\\n  - 15 tools are exposed, and there is a native JSONL contract.\\n  - Live qualification used a Luna expert (session `sess_72b9686f6177`, 8 calls) and showed Spotter works after CLIO stops.\\n  - A rejected-designs list closes the doc.\\n- **Builds on:** Flowcept and CMF, ARC (the event source), and gact-tui REST contracts. No numbered issues are cited.\\n- **Open:** acceptance gate 9 requires honest reporting of repo-wide tests, lint and type checks, and the doc does not record those results. No other open items are stated.\\n\\n## Group C: Extensions and NDP\\n\\n### 11. `extensions-discovery-and-connection.md`\\n- **Date/status:** implemented and exercised, 2026-10-26. Website publication is tracked separately.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Journey: discover → inspect → add → enable. \\\"Installed\\\", \\\"configured\\\", \\\"signed in\\\" and \\\"connected\\\" are distinct states, and \\\"connected\\\" only after a real MCP handshake.\\n  - Four views: Marketplaces, MCP connections, Skills, Plugins.\\n  - Created and uploaded items share a private-local marketplace.\\n  - OAuth reuses the MCP SDK provider; credentials are isolated by server URL and connection name.\\n  - `connection_only` keeps saved connections dormant until used by a plugin.\\n  - A common MCP presenter now emits a bounded data outline when no human content is supplied.\\n- **Builds on:** existing Store importers, the permission and resolver machinery, the `homeassistant-ai/skills` repo, and the MCP SDK OAuth provider. No numbered issues are cited.\\n- **Open:** a complete installed Desktop OAuth journey, and authorization against an actual Home Assistant deployment, \\\"remain separate acceptance work\\\". Website content is committed versus deployed to be distinguished. A manual private-GitHub backup ZIP is explicitly not synchronization.\\n\\n### 12. `ndp-connected-source.md`\\n- **Date/status:** no top-line status. Qualification dated Oct 18, 2026.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - NDP is a connected data source (Settings → Data sources and the Attach picker) with explicit Download or Link.\\n  - Paged catalog browsing runs through `asyncio.to_thread`, with a bounded IndexedDB cache.\\n  - Auth is Keycloak device flow with S256 PKCE as the public client `clio`, with tokens in the private vault.\\n  - Discovery reuses `NDPClient` from the clio-kit science MCP.\\n  - Reads route by scheme: HTTP(S), pelican/osdf, s3. Bearer is sent only beneath an explicitly configured HTTPS Endpoint, never across redirects.\\n  - There are no NDP write operations.\\n  - The generic text reader returns a bounded UTF-8 prefix for large files.\\n- **Builds on:** the pinned clio-kit science MCP, clio-schemas 0.6.0b12, and ep-api docs on GitHub. It states the `cilo`→`clio` client rename makes the earlier registration message obsolete.\\n- **Open:** protected reads still need a working Endpoint that accepts the test realm and the account's grant. A production realm needs its own registered public device-flow client. The test AAI returned no group memberships. The public catalog's full-text Solr search returned HTTP 400 at the time. A forced local expiry does not prove a real five-hour token lifetime.\\n- **Related:** pairs with `ndp-endpoint-operations.md`.\\n\\n### 13. `ndp-endpoint-operations.md`\\n- **Date/status:** live qualification 2026-10-18. No top-line status.\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Endpoints are separate from catalog datasets and sit in the \\\"Endpoints & streams\\\" tab.\\n  - Connections are per workspace and 