ment and packaged stdio.\\n  4. Image-region and A2UI selections during live inference.\\n  5. Full browser review and packaged update-channel checks.\\n  6. Integrated host qualification (packaged transport and GPU).\\n  7. The Delta run: fresh inference, token mapping and both OPAL/SPOTTER demos.\\n  - Also open: a CI-red agent head, and the DMG failure for `c6884b54`, which was not treated as a current packaging result. Core packaging omits the optional search indexer.\\n  - The doc says not to label skipped, simulated or inspection-only checks as passed.\\n\\n### 8. `blueprint-core-coordination.md`\\n**Group:** blueprint registry and clio-core coordination. **Status:** no date or status line.\\n\\n- **Decided:**\\n  - Shared blueprint-registry coordination uses Core's existing conditional scalar writes (`kPutIfAbsent` / `kPutIfVersion`) from Python. It adds no Admin service, ledger, task type or protocol.\\n  - Setup enrolls the installed registry directory with `clio blueprints setup`, and publication also guards the draft source parent.\\n  - Ownership is explicit, with no heartbeat, expiry or auto-steal. Recovery requires `clio blueprints recover --expected-owner <nonce> --owner-stopped`.\\n  - Receipts are published by an exclusive hard link, and the claim blob is never deleted.\\n- **Builds on:** Core PR #1273 (reverts the ownership service) and #1274 (exposes the existing conditionals and versioned reads). No design docs or issues are cited.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - Cross-node, shared-filesystem acceptance has **not been performed**. Only real TCP-client process tests in Core, and Agent tests with test-only conditional storage, exist.\\n  - Hosted CI must pass for the exact heads.\\n  - Not claimed: consensus across independent Core deployments, restart-safe numeric fencing, automatic failover, or protection against an external editor that ignores the guard.\\n  - A receipt does not prove the owner crashed, so recovery is manual.\\n\\n## Suggested topic groups\