e backend behind a `make_arc_store(config)` factory, is the suggested lead. Thread A, exposing ARC state over REST for the TUI, is the parallel companion.\\n- **Builds on:** `GOAL.md`, `docs/archive/arc-live-context-plane.md`, `docs/archive/implementation-spec.md` and `docs/design/compaction-checkpoint-1339.md` (#1339). The #1339 note says the v1 compaction path destroyed the human-visible transcript and amplified the `_events/m` atom lane Θ(N²) per append.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - Thread D (the CEE MCP) needs B.\\n  - Thread C (richer testing) is ongoing.\\n  - Thread E (the distributed team and the physical KV plane) is the far horizon and needs B and D.\\n  - No owners or dates are given for any thread.\\n\\n### 2. `unified-arc-highway.md`\\n**Group:** ARC / message and session unification. **Status:** first consumer live (2026-07-12; loop later replaced by `ClioReAct`). The next consumer is explicitly \\\"not started — do not claim\\\". It is an internals refactor with no `src/` change.\\n\\n- **Decided:** one operation-sourced log, with the four current stores (persistence, context, SSE and search/tree indexes) becoming thin projections of it.\\n  - The external contract is frozen: SSE vocabulary, `/messages` reload equals live, context semantics, search, trace replay, `arc.op`, compaction wire, delegation envelope, memory stats.\\n  - Migration is a 7-step strangler, one consumer at a time, with session-scoped rollback and no big-bang cutover.\\n  - The review corrected the draft in two ways. C1: a raw append lane and new message/part atom kinds are required. C2: write-path changes need a live dual-run A/B harness, because the captured corpus cannot validate them.\\n  - Ingest becomes must-succeed-or-typed-fail in the same step that removes an old write path.\\n  - Owner ruling 2026-07-12: clio-core is the default home of the log, with loud degradation to LocalFS.\\n- **Builds on:** #737 (thesis), #893 (umbrella, memory profile `893_memory_profile.md`), #889 (boot 