  "preview": "the `workflow` flow was named `plan` until a rename in Phase 5. The manifest still lists a `plan` flow under `core`, and also says \\\"named `plan` until the rename\\\", so it is partially updated.\\n- **Group:** plan and tracking. Not listed in the README.\\n\\n### 9. model-fleet.md\\n- **Decided:** model choice becomes first-class. The design has four parts: the fleet, usage, selection and the surfaces.\\n  - **Fleet:** a read model over connected accounts, served models and capability records, exposed at `GET /v1/fleet`.\\n  - **Usage:** one adapter protocol and a `UsageSnapshot`, using only CLIO's own credentials.\\n  - **Selection:** an explicit `model` on spawns, `ctx.call` and workflow steps. The order is explicit model, then `Prefers`, then the caller's model.\\n  - **Typed refusals** instead of silent replacement, a `model_choice` record on every session, and `model_exhausted` or a Question when a window runs out.\\n  - **Spending guard:** off by default for metered and credit accounts.\\n  - **Surfaces:** `list_models` and `usage` tools in a `fleet` plugin, a Usage view, a hover readout and a railroad summary.\\n  - Only children can be given a different model; there is no mid-session switch by the agent.\\n- **Builds on:** issue #1802 (the Usage UI) and quotabubble (the widget idea). It also cites `claude/sdk-plugins-flows` at `b4cf79b8`, the existing `Requires` and `Prefers` classes, and `provider.call_usage` rows.\\n- **Open:** its \\\"Open questions\\\" table has eight questions, each with a proposed default:\\n  1. An `auto` policy for picking models.\\n  2. Ordered preference lists.\\n  3. The spending-guard default.\\n  4. Who owns a cross-account choice in a workflow.\\n  5. Polling Claude and Codex usage.\\n  6. Per-session budgets, which are out of scope.\\n  7. Remote agents' fleets.\\n  8. Mid-session switching by the agent.\\n  \\n  Defaults for 1 (agent chooses), 2 (one id), 3 (as stated), 7 (each agent serves its own `/v1/fleet`, no merge) and 8 (only children) are explicit. The desktop widget is optional for 1.0.\\n- **Date/status:** Oct 22, 2026, @Jaime. \\\"Done\\\" requires M1–M12 passing.\\n- **Group:** model fleet.\\n\\n### 10. model-fleet-ledger.md\\n- **Records:** Phase 0 endpoint checks (dated 2026-10-23), decisions M-D1 to M-D14, acceptance rows M1–M12 and a Work view note.\\n  - **Endpoint checks:**\\n    - Claude passive capture was verified live, and `claude -p /usage` does not report plan windows.\\n    - Codex, OpenRouter, Anthropic and OpenAI were checked from source or docs only. Codex and OpenRouter are tested with recorded payloads.\\n  - **Decisions:**\\n    - M-D2: no Claude polling.\\n    - M-D3: an in-memory usage board.\\n    - M-D6: spend rolled up from `Session.usage_by_model`.\\n    - M-D12: Anthropic and OpenAI rate-limit headers are not captured yet.\\n    - M-D13: the `summarizer.*` config keys are deleted.\\n- **Builds on:** `model-fleet.md`, `megachange-plan.md` Phase 6, and issue iowarp/clio-agent#1837. It also cites reverted commits `0aa21aa`/`4237402`.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - M-D12 is a follow-up, tracked as #1837.\\n  - M11 is blocked on the `rlm` flow.\\n  - \\\"Tests only\\\" rows are not counted as passed: M4, M5, M7–M10.\\n  - M1 is partial because Codex, OpenRouter and vLLM have no live account.\\n  - Exhaustion and network-down cases were never exercised live.\\n- **Date/status:** checks on 2026-10-23. Live evidence is from a restart at 11:24:09 UTC on 2026-10-24, against clio-agent `ed930e0`, gact-tui `609e9461` and marketplace `bfbd3b4`. M2, M3, M6 and M12 passed live.\\n- **Group:** model fleet (tracking). Not listed in the README.\\n\\n## Suggested topic groups and reading order\\n\\n| Group | Files | Order within group |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Entry | README | 1 |\\n| Core model | plugins-and-composition, agent-sdk, plugin-change-delivery | model first, then SDK, then runtime change handling |\\n| Orchestration | orchestration-semantics | After core model |\\n| Plan and tracking | megachange-plan, removal-manifest | The plan ties the other docs together, so read it early for scope; the manifest is a lookup table |\\n| Model fleet | model-fleet, model-fleet-ledger | Design first, ledger second |\\n| Remote agents | remote-agents-and-protocols | Last; it is context, and out of scope for the change |\\n\\nThe README's own advice is to start with `megachange-plan.md`. For understanding rather than scope, plugins-and-composition then agent-sdk is the natural order.\", \"error_info\": null, \"expert_handoffs\": [], \"response_parts\": [{\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_722f5dcf58f2\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"Shell is blocked (read-only), so I'll use the file reader instead.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_88a3a563a59c\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"The previews for seven files were cut off, so I'll pull their section structure first.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_0f8e968467f2\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"The earlier reads were cut off for seven files, so I'll get their headings and the open-item passages next.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_f9ee63e24493\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"The first reads were cut off at 12,000 characters for seven of the files. I'll pull their section headings and any open-item passages with targeted searches.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_c1b48d4b6559\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"The first reads were cut off at 12,000 characters, so I'll read the missing tails of the seven files by section.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_5ce6009e46ce\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"next_thought\"}, \"text\": \"I still need three tails that the earlier reads cut off: the \\\"Deferred by design\\\" list in plugins-and-composition, the marketplace section of removal-manifest, and the end of model-fleet.\", \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"agent_id\": \"explore\", \"id\": \"part_8692397da6e1\", \"metadata\": {\"signature_field_name\": \"answer\"}, \"text\": \"# Reading guide: `design/sdk/` (10 assigned files)\\n\\nEverything below comes from files read under `/home/user/clio-agent/.cloud-run/f17/ws-f17-docs/design/sdk/`.\\n\\n**Coverage limits**\\n- `agent-sdk.md`, `plugin-change-delivery.md` and `README.md` were read in full.\\n- For the other seven, the first read was cut at 12,000 characters. I recovered their tails and open-item sections with targeted searches, so some middle sections were not read:\\n  - `orchestration-semantics.md`: \\\"Recursive and programmatic orchestration\\\", \\\"Durable execution and HPC workflows\\\", \\\"Comparison\\\", and most of \\\"Proposed semantics\\\" (lines ~66–214).\\n  - `removal-manifest.md`: the marketplace agent table after line 151.\\n  - `megachange-plan.md`: the tail of the Phase 5 live-scenario table (L9 is cut mid-row) and the Phase 5 text after it.\\n  - `model-fleet.md`: the end of the Usage view paragraph (line 123).\\n  - `model-fleet-ledger.md`: the tails of the M1–M3 and M12 rows.\\n- The shell was refused as read-only, so I have no file sizes beyond what `fs_read_file` reported.\\n\\n## How the README orders them\\n\\n`README.md` opens with \\\"Plugins, Agent SDK and flows\\\" and says to start with `megachange-plan.md`. Its table lists, in this order:\\n\\n1. megachange-plan\\n2. plugins-and-composition\\n3. agent-sdk\\n4. orchestration-semantics\\n5. model-fleet\\n6. remote-agents-and-protocols\\n7. long-term-memory-plan\\n8. memory-ledger\\n9. delegation-fork-science-plan\\n10. delegation-fork-science-addendum-a\\n\\nIt says the files were \\\"exported from the shared design docs as of Oct 20, 2026\\\", and that the repository copy is now the one to edit.\\n\\nDifferences between the README and the folder:\\n- Four assigned files are not in the README table: `plugin-change-delivery.md`, `removal-manifest.md`, `model-fleet-ledger.md` and (outside my assignment) `science-ledger.md`.\\n- `model-fleet.md` is dated Oct 22 and `megachange-plan.md` has additions dated Oct 23. Both postdate the README's stated Oct 20 export, so the README is stale.\\n\\n## Per-file summaries\\n\\n### 1. README.md\\n- **Records:** an index only. It decides nothing beyond \\\"start with megachange-plan\\\" and \\\"edit here from now on\\\".\\n- **Builds on:** the shared design docs it was exported from.\\n- **Open:** none stated.\\n- **Date/status:** exported Oct 20, 2026.\\n- **Group:** entry point.\\n\\n### 2. agent-sdk.md\\n- **Decided:** plugins hold all content, including the specific external agents they work with. Agents hold only flow, identity (`role`), plugin selection and exposure.\\n  - Python is the authoring surface, and the frozen spec produced at publish is the runtime contract.\\n  - Resolution runs twice: at publish, and at session start.\\n  - Session start expands packs, applies the user delta and override slots, checks requirements, composes the prompt and pins the result.\\n  - A required plugin can be removed, and its dependents go with it.\\n  - Hooks run child to parent.\\n  - Fragments get a soft budget of 150 tokens, as a warning only.\\n  - There is no inline agent for scripts or notebooks, and provenance is external.\\n- **Builds on:** the companion plugins/composition doc, the orchestration doc, and the \\\"Sept 17 sketch\\\". It includes a table mapping the Sept 17 fields to their new homes.\\n- **Open:** no open-questions section. Its closing section is \\\"Settled in review\\\".\\n- **Date/status:** Oct 6, 2026, @Jaime.\\n- **Group:** core model.\\n\\n### 3. plugins-and-composition.md\\n- **Decided:** the plugin is the unit of distribution, trust, composition and evolution.\\n  - It adopts Agent Plugins 1.0.0 plus the `ai.iowarp.clio` namespace, and defines composition itself because the standard has none.\\n  - An agent is a flow, an identity and a set of plugins.\\n  - Packs are membership only, and user agents are a parent plus a delta.\\n  - Agents are complete by default. Tool-name collisions are resolution errors. Hooks run child to parent.\\n  - The main prompt has five fixed sections.\\n  - External plugins are imported into the same internal record, with a trust table. Self-optimizing plugins use `evolved_from`, an override slot and a two-gate cycle.\\n- **Builds on:**\\n  - The Sept 17 planning session. A table marks each of its decisions as holds, replaced or dropped.\\n  - The Agent Plugins 1.0.0 spec.\\n  - Sister docs for the SDK, remote agents and orchestration.\\n- **Open (\\\"Deferred by design\\\"):**\\n  - Evals live in the plugin's repository and CLIO does not parse them.\\n  - The lesson-record schema and the personal marketplace come later, in the optimization campaign.\\n  - The optimizer gate \\\"depends on the benchmarks and evals work already scoped for 1.0\\\".\\n- **Date/status:** Oct 6, 2026, @Jaime.\\n- **Group:** core model.\\n\\n### 4. plugin-change-delivery.md\\n- **Decided:** adding or removing a plugin mid-conversation invalidates the provider prompt cache, so every + menu change first shows a warning.\\n  - The answer is the `apply` field of `PATCH /v1/sessions/{sid}/agent`: `now`, `compact` or `note`, or no request for \\\"No\\\".\\n  - The UI has no default. API callers who omit `apply` get `now`.\\n  - Under `note`, removed plugins stay in the prompt with a \\\"don't use\\\" note. Added plugins' fragments travel in the note, and their skills load through `load_skill`.\\n  - The note renders as a user message headed `[clio: plugin_change]` for every provider.\\n- **Builds on:** the `prompt_basis.py` owner module, provider docs for Anthropic and OpenAI (linked), and vLLM's render endpoint. It cites no earlier design docs or issues.\\n- **Open:**\\n  - Native paths are marked \\\"next step\\\": Anthropic mid-conversation system messages and `tool_addition`/`tool_removal` blocks, OpenAI `developer` messages and `additional_tools`, and a per-model capability check.\\n  - On strict open-model templates (Qwen3, vLLM, llama.cpp), tool changes have no cache-safe",
